window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1"]={"id":"CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1","title":"CGL 12 OCT 2026 SHIFT 1","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000074281","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"A train running at 72 km/h crosses a platform of length 180 m in 15 seconds. Find the length of the train. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"72 km/h की चाल से चल रही एक रेलगाड़ी 180 m लंबे प्लेटफॉर्म को 15 सेकंड में पार करती है। रेलगाड़ी की लंबाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"120 m"},"2":{"en":"180 m"},"3":{"en":"300 m"},"4":{"en":"240 m"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Speed = 72 km/h = \\(72 \\times \\frac{5}{18} = 20\\) m/s<br>Distance covered in 15 s = \\(20 \\times 15 = 300\\) m<br>Length of train = 300 − 180 = 120 m<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 120 m.</b>","hi":"चाल = 72 km/h = \\(72 \\times \\frac{5}{18} = 20\\) m/s<br>15 सेकंड में तय दूरी = \\(20 \\times 15 = 300\\) m<br>रेलगाड़ी की लंबाई = 300 − 180 = 120 m<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 120 m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000074282","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"What is the next number in the series?<br>4, 9, 14, 19, ? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"श्रेणी में अगली संख्या क्या है?<br>4, 9, 14, 19, ? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"23"},"2":{"en":"24"},"3":{"en":"25"},"4":{"en":"26"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Every term is 5 more than the previous term: 4, 9, 14, 19<br>Next term = 19 + 5 = 24<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 24.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पद पिछले पद से 5 अधिक है: 4, 9, 14, 19<br>अगला पद = 19 + 5 = 24<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 24 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000074283","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"MANGO\" is written as \"ODPJQ.\" How will \"PAPER\" be written in the same code language? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किसी निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"MANGO\" को \"ODPJQ\" लिखा जाता है। उसी कूट भाषा में \"PAPER\" को कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"RRDHT"},"2":{"en":"RDRHT"},"3":{"en":"RHRDT"},"4":{"en":"RRHDT"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The shifts alternate +2, +3: M+2=O, A+3=D, N+2=P, G+3=J, O+2=Q<br>PAPER: P+2=R, A+3=D, P+2=R, E+3=H, R+2=T<br>Code = RDRHT<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): RDRHT.</b>","hi":"स्थानांतरण बारी-बारी से +2, +3 है: M+2=O, A+3=D, N+2=P, G+3=J, O+2=Q<br>PAPER: P+2=R, A+3=D, P+2=R, E+3=H, R+2=T<br>कूट = RDRHT<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): RDRHT है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000074284","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"If 18 men or 24 women can complete a work in 20 days, in how many days will 12 men and 16 women complete the same work? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि 18 पुरुष या 24 स्त्रियाँ एक कार्य को 20 दिनों में पूरा कर सकते हैं, तो 12 पुरुष और 16 स्त्रियाँ उसी कार्य को कितने दिनों में पूरा करेंगे? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12 days","hi":"12 दिन"},"2":{"en":"13 days","hi":"13 दिन"},"3":{"en":"14 days","hi":"14 दिन"},"4":{"en":"15 days","hi":"15 दिन"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"18 men = 24 women, so 3 men = 4 women and 12 men = 16 women<br>12 men + 16 women = 16 women + 16 women = 32 women<br>24 women take 20 days, so 32 women take \\(\\frac{24 \\times 20}{32} = 15\\) days<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 15 days.</b>","hi":"18 पुरुष = 24 स्त्रियाँ, अतः 3 पुरुष = 4 स्त्रियाँ और 12 पुरुष = 16 स्त्रियाँ<br>12 पुरुष + 16 स्त्रियाँ = 16 स्त्रियाँ + 16 स्त्रियाँ = 32 स्त्रियाँ<br>24 स्त्रियाँ 20 दिन लेती हैं, अतः 32 स्त्रियाँ \\(\\frac{24 \\times 20}{32} = 15\\) दिन<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 15 दिन है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000074285","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Choose the option that perfectly matches the given address.<br><b>Original Address:</b><br>Executive Residence No. Sigma 19CRoyal Palace Residency Block XIWashington Central BoulevardLos Angeles California 90017United States of America [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"वह विकल्प चुनिए जो दिए गए पते से पूर्णतः मेल खाता है।<br><b>मूल पता:</b><br>Executive Residence No. Sigma 19CRoyal Palace Residency Block XIWashington Central BoulevardLos Angeles California 90017United States of America [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Executive Residence No. Sigma 19CRoyal Palace Residency Block XIIWashington Central BoulevardLos Angeles California 90017United States of America"},"2":{"en":"Executive Residence No. Sigma 19CRoyal Palace Residency Block XIWashington Central BoulvardLos Angeles California 90017United States of America"},"3":{"en":"Executive Residence No. Sigma 19CRoyal Palace Residency Block XIWashington Central BoulevardLos Angeles California 90107United States of America"},"4":{"en":"Executive Residence No. Sigma 19CRoyal Palace Residency Block XIWashington Central BoulevardLos Angeles California 90017United States of America"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Option 1 changes Block XI to XII, option 2 writes Boulvard, option 3 changes the PIN to 90107<br>Only option 4 keeps Block XI, Boulevard and 90017 exactly as printed<br>So it is the same address word for word<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Executive Residence No. Sigma 19CRoyal Palace Residency Block XIWashington Central BoulevardLos Angeles California 90017United States of America.</b>","hi":"विकल्प 1 में Block XI के स्थान पर XII है, विकल्प 2 में Boulvard लिखा है, विकल्प 3 में पिन 90107 है<br>केवल विकल्प 4 में Block XI, Boulevard तथा 90017 ठीक वैसे ही हैं<br>अतः यह पता शब्दशः वही है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): Executive Residence No. Sigma 19CRoyal Palace Residency Block XIWashington Central BoulevardLos Angeles California 90017United States of America है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000074286","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of numbers is given. These numbers follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing number accordingly.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">13</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">128</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">40</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये संख्याएँ पंक्ति-वार या स्तंभ-वार किसी निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करती हैं। इस पैटर्न को पहचानिए और उसके अनुसार लुप्त संख्या चुनिए।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">13</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">128</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">40</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"49"},"2":{"en":"112"},"3":{"en":"64"},"4":{"en":"144"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"In every column the bottom number is (middle)\\(^2\\) − (top)\\(^2\\)<br>Column 1: \\(12^2 - 4^2 = 144 - 16 = 128\\)<br>Column 3: \\(7^2 - 3^2 = 49 - 9 = 40\\)<br>Column 2: \\(13^2 - 5^2 = 169 - 25 = 144\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 144.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक स्तंभ में नीचे की संख्या = (मध्य)\\(^2\\) − (ऊपर)\\(^2\\)<br>स्तंभ 1: \\(12^2 - 4^2 = 144 - 16 = 128\\)<br>स्तंभ 3: \\(7^2 - 3^2 = 49 - 9 = 40\\)<br>स्तंभ 2: \\(13^2 - 5^2 = 169 - 25 = 144\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 144 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000074287","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"In a family consisting of six members P, Q, R, S, T, and U, P and R are husband and wife. Q is the eldest son of the couple. Q is married to U. S is the grandson of P and R. T is the unmarried daughter of the family. Based on the given information, identify the mother of S. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"छह सदस्यों P, Q, R, S, T और U वाले एक परिवार में, P और R पति-पत्नी हैं। Q उस दंपति का सबसे बड़ा पुत्र है। Q का विवाह U से हुआ है। S, P और R का पौत्र है। T परिवार की अविवाहित पुत्री है। दी गई जानकारी के आधार पर S की माता पहचानिए। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"U"},"2":{"en":"T"},"3":{"en":"R"},"4":{"en":"Q"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"162\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 162\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"135\" y=\"62\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"109\" y=\"116\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M135 14H157M135 18H157M111 68H133M111 72H133M146 18V50M96 50H197M96 50V62M197 50V62M122 72V104M122 104V116\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"120\" y=\"22\">P+</text><text x=\"173\" y=\"22\">R−</text><text x=\"96\" y=\"76\">Q+</text><text x=\"148\" y=\"76\">U−</text><text x=\"197\" y=\"76\">T−</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"130\">S+</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"157\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></svg><br>S is the son of Q and his wife U, so U is the mother of S.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): U.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"162\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 162\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"135\" y=\"62\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"109\" y=\"116\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M135 14H157M135 18H157M111 68H133M111 72H133M146 18V50M96 50H197M96 50V62M197 50V62M122 72V104M122 104V116\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"120\" y=\"22\">P+</text><text x=\"173\" y=\"22\">R−</text><text x=\"96\" y=\"76\">Q+</text><text x=\"148\" y=\"76\">U−</text><text x=\"197\" y=\"76\">T−</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"130\">S+</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"157\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ पुरुष  − स्त्री  — भाई-बहन  = पति-पत्नी  | पीढ़ी</text></svg><br>S, Q तथा उसकी पत्नी U का पुत्र है, अतः U, S की माता है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): U है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000074288","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Study the pattern in the given series and find the next set of letters in the series.<br>PTI, LUE, HVA, ? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दी गई श्रेणी का पैटर्न अध्ययन कीजिए और श्रेणी में अक्षरों का अगला समूह ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>PTI, LUE, HVA, ? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"DWW"},"2":{"en":"DWU"},"3":{"en":"ROV"},"4":{"en":"RWV"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"First letters P, L, H go 4 back each time, so next is D<br>Second letters T, U, V go 1 forward, so next is W<br>Third letters I, E, A go 4 back each time, so next is W<br>Next group = DWW<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): DWW.</b>","hi":"पहले अक्षर P, L, H हर बार 4 पीछे, अतः अगला D<br>दूसरे अक्षर T, U, V हर बार 1 आगे, अतः अगला W<br>तीसरे अक्षर I, E, A हर बार 4 पीछे, अतः अगला W<br>अगला समूह = DWW<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): DWW है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000074289","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Roll numbers are generated where the middle digit is the remainder of the first digit divided by the last digit. Which entry is invalid? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"रोल नंबर इस प्रकार बनाए जाते हैं कि मध्य अंक, पहले अंक को अंतिम अंक से भाग देने पर प्राप्त शेषफल होता है। कौन-सी प्रविष्टि अमान्य है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"713"},"2":{"en":"826"},"3":{"en":"914"},"4":{"en":"532"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"713: 7 ÷ 3 leaves remainder 1 ✔<br>826: 8 ÷ 6 leaves remainder 2 ✔<br>914: 9 ÷ 4 leaves remainder 1 ✔<br>532: 5 ÷ 2 leaves remainder 1, not 3 ✘<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 532.</b>","hi":"713: 7 ÷ 3 का शेषफल 1 ✔<br>826: 8 ÷ 6 का शेषफल 2 ✔<br>914: 9 ÷ 4 का शेषफल 1 ✔<br>532: 5 ÷ 2 का शेषफल 1 है, 3 नहीं ✘<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 532 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000074290","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"Your department is experiencing high work pressure because of tight project schedules and increased workload. In this situation, you observe that one of your team members is consistently failing to meet deadlines and appears withdrawn and less engaged than usual. As the team leader, what is the most appropriate way to handle this situation? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"आपका विभाग कड़े प्रोजेक्ट शेड्यूल और बढ़े हुए कार्यभार के कारण अत्यधिक कार्यदबाव में है। इस स्थिति में आप देखते हैं कि आपके दल का एक सदस्य लगातार समय-सीमा पूरी नहीं कर पा रहा है और सामान्य से अधिक अलग-थलग तथा कम सक्रिय दिख रहा है। दल के नेता के रूप में इस स्थिति से निपटने का सबसे उपयुक्त तरीका क्या है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Issue an official show-cause notice immediately so that the employee’s performance issue is formally documented and appropriately addressed.","hi":"कर्मचारी के प्रदर्शन की समस्या को औपचारिक रूप से दर्ज करने और उचित रूप से निपटने के लिए तुरंत आधिकारिक कारण-बताओ नोटिस जारी करें।"},"2":{"en":"Conduct an empathetic individual conversation with the employee to identify the underlying causes of the performance concerns in detail.","hi":"प्रदर्शन संबंधी चिंताओं के मूल कारणों को विस्तार से जानने के लिए कर्मचारी से सहानुभूतिपूर्ण व्यक्तिगत बातचीत करें।"},"3":{"en":"Arrange a meeting to inform the team member that their recent performance is unacceptable and that they are being placed on a formal performance improvement plan immediately.","hi":"दल के सदस्य को सूचित करने के लिए बैठक आयोजित करें कि उसका हालिया प्रदर्शन अस्वीकार्य है और उसे तुरंत औपचारिक प्रदर्शन सुधार योजना में रखा जा रहा है।"},"4":{"en":"Reassign the pending tasks to other team members without informing the employee who is currently responsible for them.","hi":"जो कर्मचारी वर्तमान में उन कार्यों के लिए उत्तरदायी है, उसे बिना बताए लंबित कार्य अन्य दल के सदस्यों को सौंप दें।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The member is withdrawn because of work pressure, so the cause has to be found first<br>A private, empathetic conversation brings out the real problem before any action<br>Punitive or secret steps would only worsen the situation<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Conduct an empathetic individual conversation with the employee to identify the underlying causes of the performance concerns in detail.</b>","hi":"सदस्य कार्यदबाव के कारण अलग-थलग है, अतः पहले कारण जानना आवश्यक है<br>निजी और सहानुभूतिपूर्ण बातचीत से वास्तविक समस्या सामने आती है<br>दंडात्मक या गुप्त कदम स्थिति को और बिगाड़ देंगे<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): प्रदर्शन संबंधी चिंताओं के मूल कारणों को विस्तार से जानने के लिए कर्मचारी से सहानुभूतिपूर्ण व्यक्तिगत बातचीत करें। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000074291","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"A dedicated team member has been consistently underperforming on shared tasks for the past two weeks, appearing distracted and tired during office hours. Which of the following actions represents the most constructive way to address this shift in their professional behavior? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक समर्पित दल सदस्य पिछले दो सप्ताह से साझा कार्यों में लगातार कम प्रदर्शन कर रहा है और कार्यालय समय में अन्यमनस्क तथा थका हुआ दिख रहा है। उसके व्यावसायिक व्यवहार में इस बदलाव से निपटने का सबसे रचनात्मक तरीका निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Approach them privately to express concern and ask if they are facing any professional challenges.","hi":"चिंता व्यक्त करने और यह पूछने के लिए उनसे निजी रूप से मिलें कि क्या वे कोई व्यावसायिक कठिनाई झेल रहे हैं।"},"2":{"en":"Criticize their lack of focus openly during a team meeting to encourage immediate improvement.","hi":"तत्काल सुधार के लिए दल की बैठक में खुलकर उनकी एकाग्रता की कमी की आलोचना करें।"},"3":{"en":"Formally escalate the observed performance issues to the department head without initiating a conversation.","hi":"बातचीत शुरू किए बिना देखी गई प्रदर्शन समस्याओं को औपचारिक रूप से विभागाध्यक्ष तक पहुँचाएँ।"},"4":{"en":"Reduce your collaborative efforts with them to minimize the impact of their errors on your work.","hi":"उनकी गलतियों का आपके कार्य पर पड़ने वाला प्रभाव कम करने के लिए उनके साथ सहयोग कम कर दें।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The person was sincere earlier, so the change points to a problem behind it<br>A private talk protects dignity and finds the cause<br>Public criticism, escalation or withdrawal would harm both trust and work<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Approach them privately to express concern and ask if they are facing any professional challenges.</b>","hi":"व्यक्ति पहले समर्पित था, अतः बदलाव किसी समस्या की ओर संकेत करता है<br>निजी बातचीत सम्मान बचाते हुए कारण जानती है<br>सार्वजनिक आलोचना, शिकायत या दूरी बना लेना विश्वास और कार्य दोनों को हानि पहुँचाएगा<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): चिंता व्यक्त करने और यह पूछने के लिए उनसे निजी रूप से मिलें कि क्या वे कोई व्यावसायिक कठिनाई झेल रहे हैं। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000074292","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter/Alphabetical Analogy","question":{"en":"What should come in place of question mark (?) in the following analogy?<br>C3F : F6I :: I9L : ? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित सादृश्य में प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर क्या आएगा?<br>C3F : F6I :: I9L : ? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"M12O"},"2":{"en":"L12O"},"3":{"en":"L11O"},"4":{"en":"L12N"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Each term is letter – number – letter, with the two letters three places apart<br>C3F, F6I, I9L: letters move 3 forward and the number rises by 3 each time<br>Next term = L12O<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): L12O.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पद अक्षर – संख्या – अक्षर है और दोनों अक्षर तीन स्थान दूर हैं<br>C3F, F6I, I9L: अक्षर हर बार 3 आगे बढ़ते हैं और संख्या 3 बढ़ती है<br>अगला पद = L12O<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): L12O है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000074293","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the given question, a few statements have been given followed by conclusions based on them. Consider the statements to be true and answer which of the given conclusions logically follow the statement.<br><b>Statements</b><br>1. All stars are celestial objects.<br>2. All celestial objects that emit light are visible.<br>3. Some stars do not emit light.<br><b>Conclusions</b><br>I. Some stars are not visible.<br>II. All stars that emit light are visible.<br>III. Some celestial objects are not visible.<br>IV. All visible objects are celestial objects. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिए गए प्रश्न में कुछ कथन और उनके आधार पर निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। कथनों को सत्य मानिए और बताइए कि दिए गए निष्कर्षों में से कौन-से तार्किक रूप से कथन का अनुसरण करते हैं।<br><b>कथन</b><br>1. सभी तारे खगोलीय पिंड हैं।<br>2. प्रकाश उत्सर्जित करने वाले सभी खगोलीय पिंड दृश्यमान हैं।<br>3. कुछ तारे प्रकाश उत्सर्जित नहीं करते।<br><b>निष्कर्ष</b><br>I. कुछ तारे दृश्यमान नहीं हैं।<br>II. प्रकाश उत्सर्जित करने वाले सभी तारे दृश्यमान हैं।<br>III. कुछ खगोलीय पिंड दृश्यमान नहीं हैं।<br>IV. सभी दृश्यमान पिंड खगोलीय पिंड हैं। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I, II and III follow","hi":"केवल I, II और III अनुसरण करते हैं"},"2":{"en":"Only II and III follow","hi":"केवल II और III अनुसरण करते हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only II follow","hi":"केवल II अनुसरण करता है"},"4":{"en":"All four follow","hi":"सभी चारों अनुसरण करते हैं"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Star → celestial object; (celestial object + emits light) → visible<br>So every star that emits light is visible, which is conclusion II<br>A star without light may still be visible, so I and III need not follow, and IV reverses the given relation<br>Only II follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Only II follow.</b>","hi":"तारा → खगोलीय पिंड; (खगोलीय पिंड + प्रकाश उत्सर्जक) → दृश्यमान<br>अतः प्रकाश उत्सर्जित करने वाला प्रत्येक तारा दृश्यमान है, यही निष्कर्ष II है<br>प्रकाश न देने वाला तारा भी दृश्यमान हो सकता है, अतः I तथा III आवश्यक नहीं, और IV दिए संबंध को उलट देता है<br>केवल II अनुसरण करता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): केवल II अनुसरण करता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000074294","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"In the following question, one statement is given, followed by certain inferences. Consider the statement to be true even if it seems to contradict commonly known facts. Read the inferences carefully and decide which of them logically follow from the given statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>Heavy pesticide use in farming pollutes soil and water, persists in crops, and eventually enters the food chain, posing a risk to human health.<br><b>Inferences:</b><br>I. Overuse of pesticides in agriculture is harmful to human beings.<br>II. Excessive pesticide use can adversely impact water quality. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन और उसके बाद कुछ अनुमान दिए गए हैं। कथन को सत्य मानिए, भले ही वह सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों के विपरीत प्रतीत हो। अनुमानों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि उनमें से कौन-से तार्किक रूप से दिए गए कथन से निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>खेती में कीटनाशकों का अत्यधिक उपयोग मिट्टी और जल को प्रदूषित करता है, फसलों में बना रहता है और अंततः खाद्य शृंखला में प्रवेश कर मानव स्वास्थ्य के लिए जोखिम पैदा करता है।<br><b>अनुमान:</b><br>I. कृषि में कीटनाशकों का अत्यधिक उपयोग मनुष्यों के लिए हानिकारक है।<br>II. कीटनाशकों का अत्यधिक उपयोग जल की गुणवत्ता पर प्रतिकूल प्रभाव डाल सकता है। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Inference I follows.","hi":"केवल अनुमान I निकलता है।"},"2":{"en":"Only Inference II follows.","hi":"केवल अनुमान II निकलता है।"},"3":{"en":"Both Inferences I and II follow.","hi":"अनुमान I और II दोनों निकलते हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Neither Inference I nor Inference II follows.","hi":"न तो अनुमान I और न ही अनुमान II निकलता है।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The statement directly says the pesticide residue enters the food chain and risks human health, so I follows<br>It also says soil and water get polluted, so II follows<br>Both inferences follow<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Both Inferences I and II follow.</b>","hi":"कथन सीधे कहता है कि कीटनाशक अवशेष खाद्य शृंखला में जाकर मानव स्वास्थ्य के लिए जोखिम हैं, अतः I निकलता है<br>यह भी कहा गया है कि मिट्टी और जल प्रदूषित होते हैं, अतः II निकलता है<br>दोनों अनुमान निकलते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): अनुमान I और II दोनों निकलते हैं। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000074295","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Among the four given combinations, one has error. Identify it<br>(a) Rohanshi Mehta, 18-C Ocean View Colony, 10<sup>th</sup> cross road, Udaipur, 9871203456, 313001<br>(b) Rohanshi Mehta, 18-C Ocean View Colony, 10<sup>th</sup> cross road, Udaipur, 9871203456, 313001<br>(c) Rohanshi Mehta, 18-C Oceanview Colony, 10<sup>th</sup> cross road, Udaipur, 9871203456, 313001<br>(d) Rohanshi Mehta, 18-C Ocean View Colony, 10<sup>th</sup> cross road, Udaipur, 9871203456, 313001 [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिए गए चार संयोजनों में से एक में त्रुटि है। उसे पहचानिए<br>(a) Rohanshi Mehta, 18-C Ocean View Colony, 10<sup>th</sup> cross road, Udaipur, 9871203456, 313001<br>(b) Rohanshi Mehta, 18-C Ocean View Colony, 10<sup>th</sup> cross road, Udaipur, 9871203456, 313001<br>(c) Rohanshi Mehta, 18-C Oceanview Colony, 10<sup>th</sup> cross road, Udaipur, 9871203456, 313001<br>(d) Rohanshi Mehta, 18-C Ocean View Colony, 10<sup>th</sup> cross road, Udaipur, 9871203456, 313001 [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"a"},"2":{"en":"b"},"3":{"en":"c"},"4":{"en":"d"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Options (a), (b) and (d) are identical, with the colony written as Ocean View Colony<br>Option (c) writes it as Oceanview Colony, without the space<br>So (c) carries the error<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): c.</b>","hi":"विकल्प (a), (b) और (d) एक जैसे हैं, जिनमें कॉलोनी Ocean View Colony लिखी है<br>विकल्प (c) में इसे बिना अंतराल के Oceanview Colony लिखा है<br>अतः त्रुटि (c) में है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): c है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000074296","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Choose the option which is exactly similar to: 20-09-2026, 54/3, Palm Beach Road, Vashi, Navi Mumbai-400703 [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"उस विकल्प को चुनिए जो ठीक इसके समान है: 20-09-2026, 54/3, Palm Beach Road, Vashi, Navi Mumbai-400703 [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"20-09-2026, 54/3, Palm Beach Road, Vashi, Navi Mumbai-400703"},"2":{"en":"20-09-2026, 54/3, Palm Beach Road, Vashi, Navi Mumbai 400703"},"3":{"en":"09-09-2026, 54/3, Palm Beach Road, Vashi, Navi Mumbai-400703"},"4":{"en":"19-09-2025, 54/3, Palm Beach Road, Vashi, Navi Mumbai-400703"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Option 2 drops the hyphen before the PIN, option 3 changes the date to 09-09-2026, option 4 changes it to 19-09-2025<br>Option 1 keeps the date 20-09-2026 and the written form Navi Mumbai-400703 exactly<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 20-09-2026, 54/3, Palm Beach Road, Vashi, Navi Mumbai-400703.</b>","hi":"विकल्प 2 में पिन से पहले का हाइफ़न हटा है, विकल्प 3 में तिथि 09-09-2026 है, विकल्प 4 में तिथि 19-09-2025 है<br>विकल्प 1 में तिथि 20-09-2026 तथा Navi Mumbai-400703 ठीक वैसा ही है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 20-09-2026, 54/3, Palm Beach Road, Vashi, Navi Mumbai-400703 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000074297","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"During an annual performance review, an employee receives highly critical feedback from their supervisor regarding their project management skills. The employee strongly disagrees with this assessment and believes it overlooks major successes.<br><br>Which of the following responses best demonstrates high emotional intelligence (EI)? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"वार्षिक प्रदर्शन समीक्षा के दौरान एक कर्मचारी को उसके पर्यवेक्षक से परियोजना प्रबंधन कौशल पर कड़ी आलोचनात्मक प्रतिक्रिया मिलती है। कर्मचारी इस मूल्यांकन से सहमत नहीं है और मानता है कि इसमें उसकी बड़ी सफलताओं को अनदेखा किया गया है।<br><br>निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी प्रतिक्रिया उच्च भावनात्मक बुद्धिमत्ता (EI) को सबसे अच्छी तरह दर्शाती है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Immediately interrupting the supervisor to counter each criticism with verbal evidence and defensive explanations.","hi":"प्रत्येक आलोचना का मौखिक प्रमाण और बचावपूर्ण स्पष्टीकरण देकर तुरंत जवाब देने के लिए पर्यवेक्षक को टोकना।"},"2":{"en":"Actively listening to the entire evaluation without interrupting, asking objective clarifying questions for specific examples, and requesting a follow-up meeting after a few days to provide a considered response.","hi":"बिना टोके पूरा मूल्यांकन ध्यान से सुनना, विशिष्ट उदाहरणों के लिए वस्तुनिष्ठ स्पष्टीकरण पूछना और कुछ दिनों बाद सोच-विचार कर उत्तर देने के लिए अनुवर्ती बैठक का अनुरोध करना।"},"3":{"en":"Submissively accepting all the negative criticism without question or clarification simply to prevent a professional conflict or argument.","hi":"व्यावसायिक टकराव या बहस से बचने के लिए बिना प्रश्न या स्पष्टीकरण के सभी नकारात्मक आलोचनाओं को चुपचाप स्वीकार कर लेना।"},"4":{"en":"Explicitly telling the supervisor that the feedback is completely unfair, biased, and clearly based on a fundamental misunderstanding of their actual work.","hi":"पर्यवेक्षक को स्पष्ट रूप से बताना कि प्रतिक्रिया पूरी तरह अनुचित, पक्षपातपूर्ण और उनके वास्तविक कार्य की मूलभूत गलतफहमी पर आधारित है।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Emotional intelligence means controlling the first reaction and understanding the feedback<br>Listening fully, asking for specific examples and replying after reflection keeps the discussion objective<br>Interrupting, silent surrender and open accusation are all reactive<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Actively listening to the entire evaluation without interrupting, asking objective clarifying questions for specific examples, and requesting a follow-up meeting after a few days to provide a considered response.</b>","hi":"भावनात्मक बुद्धिमत्ता का अर्थ है पहली प्रतिक्रिया पर नियंत्रण और प्रतिक्रिया को समझना<br>पूरा सुनना, ठोस उदाहरण पूछना और सोच-विचार कर उत्तर देना चर्चा को वस्तुनिष्ठ रखता है<br>टोकना, चुपचाप स्वीकार करना और खुला आरोप लगाना सभी प्रतिक्रियात्मक हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): बिना टोके पूरा मूल्यांकन ध्यान से सुनना, विशिष्ट उदाहरणों के लिए वस्तुनिष्ठ स्पष्टीकरण पूछना और कुछ दिनों बाद सोच-विचार कर उत्तर देने के लिए अनुवर्ती बैठक का अनुरोध करना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000074298","section":"REASONING","topic":"Eligibility","question":{"en":"Read the given conditions carefully and determine the appropriate outcome for the case provided. If any exception applies, identify the authority to whom the case should be referred.<br><b>Criteria for Specialized Software Training Entry:</b><br>(i) Must be proficient in Java.<br>(ii) Must have passed the internal aptitude test.<br><b>Exceptions:</b><br><b>Exception (A):</b> If the candidate has zero Java knowledge but passed the aptitude test with distinction, refer the case to the Program Manager.<br><b>Exception (B):</b> If the candidate meets criteria (i) and (ii) but has a history of training program withdrawal, refer the case to the Training Director.<br><b>Case:</b> The candidate has no Java knowledge and passed the internal aptitude test with distinction. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दी गई शर्तों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और दिए गए मामले के लिए उपयुक्त परिणाम निर्धारित कीजिए। यदि कोई अपवाद लागू होता है, तो वह प्राधिकारी पहचानिए जिसे मामला भेजा जाना चाहिए।<br><b>विशिष्ट सॉफ्टवेयर प्रशिक्षण प्रवेश के मानदंड:</b><br>(i) जावा में दक्ष होना चाहिए।<br>(ii) आंतरिक अभिक्षमता परीक्षा उत्तीर्ण होनी चाहिए।<br><b>अपवाद:</b><br><b>अपवाद (A):</b> यदि अभ्यर्थी को जावा का बिल्कुल ज्ञान नहीं है परंतु उसने अभिक्षमता परीक्षा विशिष्टता के साथ उत्तीर्ण की है, तो मामला कार्यक्रम प्रबंधक को भेजें।<br><b>अपवाद (B):</b> यदि अभ्यर्थी मानदंड (i) और (ii) पूरा करता है परंतु प्रशिक्षण कार्यक्रम छोड़ने का इतिहास है, तो मामला प्रशिक्षण निदेशक को भेजें।<br><b>मामला:</b> अभ्यर्थी को जावा का ज्ञान नहीं है और उसने आंतरिक अभिक्षमता परीक्षा विशिष्टता के साथ उत्तीर्ण की है। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Entry to be granted","hi":"प्रवेश दिया जाए"},"2":{"en":"Case to be referred to the Program Manager","hi":"मामला कार्यक्रम प्रबंधक को भेजा जाए"},"3":{"en":"Application to be rejected","hi":"आवेदन अस्वीकार किया जाए"},"4":{"en":"Case to be referred to the Training Director","hi":"मामला प्रशिक्षण निदेशक को भेजा जाए"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Criterion (i) is not met, as the candidate has zero Java knowledge<br>But the aptitude test is passed with distinction, which is exactly Exception (A)<br>So the case goes to the Program Manager<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Case to be referred to the Program Manager.</b>","hi":"मानदंड (i) पूरा नहीं होता, क्योंकि अभ्यर्थी को जावा का ज्ञान नहीं है<br>परंतु अभिक्षमता परीक्षा विशिष्टता के साथ उत्तीर्ण है, जो ठीक अपवाद (A) है<br>अतः मामला कार्यक्रम प्रबंधक को भेजा जाए<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): मामला कार्यक्रम प्रबंधक को भेजा जाए है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000074299","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>A space agency has initiated long-duration orbital missions to study microgravity effects on human physiology and spacecraft systems.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Microgravity may have measurable effects on human biological systems.<br>II. Space missions are conducted only for entertainment purposes. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और उसे सत्य मानिए। फिर उसके नीचे दिए दो निष्कर्षों को देखिए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सा निष्कर्ष, यदि कोई हो, तार्किक रूप से कथन से निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>एक अंतरिक्ष एजेंसी ने मानव शरीरक्रिया और अंतरिक्ष यान प्रणालियों पर सूक्ष्मगुरुत्व के प्रभावों के अध्ययन के लिए दीर्घकालिक कक्षीय मिशन शुरू किए हैं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. सूक्ष्मगुरुत्व का मानव जैविक तंत्रों पर मापने योग्य प्रभाव हो सकता है।<br>II. अंतरिक्ष मिशन केवल मनोरंजन के उद्देश्य से किए जाते हैं। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor conclusion II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Studying microgravity effects on human physiology means those effects are measurable, so I follows<br>Nothing in the statement supports entertainment as the only purpose, so II does not follow<br>Only conclusion I follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only conclusion I follows.</b>","hi":"मानव शरीरक्रिया पर सूक्ष्मगुरुत्व के प्रभावों का अध्ययन करना दर्शाता है कि वे प्रभाव मापने योग्य हैं, अतः I निकलता है<br>कथन में मनोरंजन को एकमात्र उद्देश्य बताने का कोई आधार नहीं, अतः II नहीं निकलता<br>केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000074300","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"LIGHTS\" is written as \"LjGiTt\". How will \"WINDOW\" be written in the same code language? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किसी निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"LIGHTS\" को \"LjGiTt\" लिखा जाता है। उसी कूट भाषा में \"WINDOW\" को कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"WkNoOx"},"2":{"en":"WjNeOx"},"3":{"en":"WkNfOx"},"4":{"en":"WjNeOy"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Odd-placed letters stay unchanged, even-placed letters move one step forward and become small: L-i-G-i-T-t<br>WINDOW: W, I → j, N, D → e, O, W → x<br>Code = WjNeOx<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): WjNeOx.</b>","hi":"विषम स्थान के अक्षर अपरिवर्तित रहते हैं, सम स्थान के अक्षर एक आगे बढ़कर छोटे हो जाते हैं: L-i-G-i-T-t<br>WINDOW: W, I → j, N, D → e, O, W → x<br>कूट = WjNeOx<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): WjNeOx है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000074301","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, if fGhIj is written as gJiLk, then how will mNoPq be written in that same code language? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किसी निश्चित कूट भाषा में यदि fGhIj को gJiLk लिखा जाता है, तो उसी कूट भाषा में mNoPq को कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"nRrSt"},"2":{"en":"nQpSq"},"3":{"en":"nQpSr"},"4":{"en":"mPqSq"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The shifts alternate +1, +3 and each letter keeps its case: f+1=g, G+3=J, h+1=i, I+3=L, j+1=k<br>mNoPq: m+1=n, N+3=Q, o+1=p, P+3=S, q+1=r<br>Code = nQpSr<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): nQpSr.</b>","hi":"स्थानांतरण बारी-बारी से +1, +3 है और प्रत्येक अक्षर का केस वही रहता है: f+1=g, G+3=J, h+1=i, I+3=L, j+1=k<br>mNoPq: m+1=n, N+3=Q, o+1=p, P+3=S, q+1=r<br>कूट = nQpSr<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): nQpSr है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000074302","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"Direction:<br>Choose the most suitable decision based on the scenario provided below.<br><br>Scenario: A university receives evidence that a highly successful research project contains a minor methodological flaw. The flaw does not invalidate the main findings but affects one secondary analysis. The project has already attracted substantial funding. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निर्देश:<br>नीचे दिए गए परिदृश्य के आधार पर सबसे उपयुक्त निर्णय चुनिए।<br><br>परिदृश्य: एक विश्वविद्यालय को साक्ष्य मिलता है कि एक अत्यंत सफल शोध परियोजना में एक छोटी कार्यप्रणालीगत त्रुटि है। यह त्रुटि मुख्य निष्कर्षों को अमान्य नहीं करती परंतु एक गौण विश्लेषण को प्रभावित करती है। परियोजना को पहले ही पर्याप्त वित्तपोषण मिल चुका है। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Withhold the information until future studies provide additional evidence.","hi":"अतिरिक्त साक्ष्य मिलने तक जानकारी रोक कर रखें।"},"2":{"en":"Publicly disclose the issue, correct the affected analysis, and maintain transparency.","hi":"समस्या सार्वजनिक रूप से बताएँ, प्रभावित विश्लेषण सुधारें और पारदर्शिता बनाए रखें।"},"3":{"en":"Cancel the entire project because any methodological flaw is unacceptable.","hi":"पूरी परियोजना रद्द कर दें, क्योंकि कोई भी कार्यप्रणालीगत त्रुटि अस्वीकार्य है।"},"4":{"en":"Ignore the issue because the primary findings remain unaffected.","hi":"समस्या को अनदेखा करें, क्योंकि मुख्य निष्कर्ष अप्रभावित हैं।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The flaw is real but limited to one secondary analysis<br>Academic honesty needs disclosure and correction rather than concealment or cancellation<br>Transparency with correction keeps both the work and the funding credible<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Publicly disclose the issue, correct the affected analysis, and maintain transparency.</b>","hi":"त्रुटि वास्तविक है परंतु केवल एक गौण विश्लेषण तक सीमित है<br>शैक्षणिक ईमानदारी के लिए छिपाने या रद्द करने के बजाय बताना और सुधारना आवश्यक है<br>पारदर्शिता और सुधार से कार्य तथा वित्तपोषण दोनों की विश्वसनीयता बनी रहती है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): समस्या सार्वजनिक रूप से बताएँ, प्रभावित विश्लेषण सुधारें और पारदर्शिता बनाए रखें। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000074303","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"The regional park authority has prohibited the use of all artificial lighting within the sanctuary to protect the natural nocturnal habitat of local endangered species. Which assumption underlies this prohibition? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"क्षेत्रीय उद्यान प्राधिकरण ने स्थानीय संकटग्रस्त प्रजातियों के प्राकृतिक रात्रिचर आवास की रक्षा के लिए अभयारण्य के भीतर सभी कृत्रिम प्रकाश के उपयोग पर प्रतिबंध लगा दिया है। इस प्रतिबंध का आधार कौन-सी मान्यता है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Visitors will strictly adhere to the lighting ban, making additional monitoring measures unnecessary.","hi":"आगंतुक प्रकाश प्रतिबंध का कड़ाई से पालन करेंगे, जिससे अतिरिक्त निगरानी उपायों की आवश्यकता नहीं रहेगी।"},"2":{"en":"Implementing this ban will immediately result in a significant increase in the local species population.","hi":"इस प्रतिबंध के लागू होने से स्थानीय प्रजातियों की संख्या में तुरंत महत्वपूर्ण वृद्धि होगी।"},"3":{"en":"The current levels of artificial light are the only threats facing these species within the sanctuary.","hi":"अभयारण्य के भीतर इन प्रजातियों के सामने कृत्रिम प्रकाश का वर्तमान स्तर ही एकमात्र खतरा है।"},"4":{"en":"Artificial light exposure negatively impacts the mating and hunting behaviors of these endangered species.","hi":"कृत्रिम प्रकाश के संपर्क से इन संकटग्रस्त प्रजातियों के साथी-चयन तथा शिकार व्यवहार पर नकारात्मक प्रभाव पड़ता है।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"A ban on light is imposed only because light itself disturbs these animals<br>So the hidden assumption is that artificial light harms their mating and hunting<br>The other three go beyond the statement: enforcement, immediate population rise, or a single threat<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Artificial light exposure negatively impacts the mating and hunting behaviors of these endangered species.</b>","hi":"प्रकाश पर प्रतिबंध इसलिए लगाया जाता है क्योंकि प्रकाश स्वयं इन जीवों को बाधित करता है<br>अतः छिपी मान्यता यह है कि कृत्रिम प्रकाश उनके साथी-चयन और शिकार को हानि पहुँचाता है<br>शेष तीन कथन से आगे जाते हैं: पालन, तत्काल संख्या-वृद्धि या एकमात्र खतरा<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): कृत्रिम प्रकाश के संपर्क से इन संकटग्रस्त प्रजातियों के साथी-चयन तथा शिकार व्यवहार पर नकारात्मक प्रभाव पड़ता है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000074304","section":"REASONING","topic":"Matrix","question":{"en":"Which of the following rows/columns are connected/related with each other in some way?<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Rows</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">27</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">18</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">36</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">45</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">18</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">20</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी पंक्तियाँ/स्तंभ किसी प्रकार एक-दूसरे से संबंधित हैं?<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Rows</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">27</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">18</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">36</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">45</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">18</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">20</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rows I, III and V","hi":"पंक्तियाँ I, III और V"},"2":{"en":"Rows II, IV and V","hi":"पंक्तियाँ II, IV और V"},"3":{"en":"Rows I, II and III","hi":"पंक्तियाँ I, II और III"},"4":{"en":"Rows I, II and IV","hi":"पंक्तियाँ I, II और IV"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Row I ÷ 3 gives row III: 27, 18, 36, 45, 9 → 9, 6, 12, 15, 3<br>Row III ÷ 3 gives row V: 9, 6, 12, 15, 3 → 3, 2, 4, 5, 1<br>So rows I, III and V follow one pattern, while rows II and IV do not divide in the same way<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Rows I, III and V.</b>","hi":"पंक्ति I ÷ 3 से पंक्ति III: 27, 18, 36, 45, 9 → 9, 6, 12, 15, 3<br>पंक्ति III ÷ 3 से पंक्ति V: 9, 6, 12, 15, 3 → 3, 2, 4, 5, 1<br>अतः पंक्तियाँ I, III तथा V एक ही पैटर्न का पालन करती हैं, जबकि पंक्तियाँ II और IV इस प्रकार विभाजित नहीं होतीं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): पंक्तियाँ I, III और V है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000074305","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Analogy","question":{"en":"Select the option that is related to the third word in the same way as the second word is related to the first word. (The words must be considered as meaningful English words and must not be related to each other based on the number of letters/number of consonants/vowels in the word.)<br>Hive : Bees :: Anthill : ? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"उस विकल्प का चयन कीजिए जो तीसरे शब्द से उसी प्रकार संबंधित है जिस प्रकार दूसरा शब्द पहले शब्द से संबंधित है। (शब्दों को अर्थपूर्ण अंग्रेज़ी शब्द मानना है और उन्हें अक्षरों की संख्या/व्यंजनों/स्वरों की संख्या के आधार पर एक-दूसरे से संबंधित नहीं मानना है।)<br>Hive : Bees :: Anthill : ? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ants","hi":"चींटियाँ"},"2":{"en":"Beetles","hi":"भृंग"},"3":{"en":"Spiders","hi":"मकड़ियाँ"},"4":{"en":"Butterflies","hi":"तितलियाँ"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"A hive is the dwelling of bees<br>In the same way an anthill is the dwelling of ants<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Ants.</b>","hi":"छत्ता मधुमक्खियों का निवास है<br>उसी प्रकार बाँबी चींटियों का निवास है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): चींटियाँ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000074306","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Microeconomics","question":{"en":"Which of the following is the correct explanation of a consumer surplus? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन उपभोक्ता अधिशेष (consumer surplus) की सही व्याख्या है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"What the consumer pays (-) what it is worth","hi":"उपभोक्ता जो भुगतान करता है (-) जो उसका मूल्य है"},"2":{"en":"What the consumer is ready to pay (-) what they actually pay","hi":"उपभोक्ता जो भुगतान करने को तैयार है (-) जो वह वास्तव में भुगतान करता है"},"3":{"en":"What the seller quotes as the price (-) what the consumer actually pays","hi":"विक्रेता जो मूल्य बताता है (-) उपभोक्ता जो वास्तव में भुगतान करता है"},"4":{"en":"What the seller quotes as the price (-) cost of manufacturing to the seller","hi":"विक्रेता जो मूल्य बताता है (-) विक्रेता की विनिर्माण लागत"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – What the consumer is ready to pay (-) what they actually pay</b><br>Consumer surplus is the difference between the <b>price a consumer is willing to pay</b> for a good and the <b>price he actually pays</b>. It measures the extra satisfaction or welfare the consumer gains from a purchase and is shown as the area below the demand curve and above the market price.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The concept was introduced by <b>Alfred Marshall</b>; consumer surplus = Total utility − (Price × Quantity).<br>• The demand curve shows the maximum willingness to pay, so the area above the price line and below the demand curve is consumer surplus.<br>• <b>Producer surplus</b> is the difference between the price received by the seller and the minimum price at which he is willing to sell.<br>• In a perfectly competitive market, total welfare = consumer surplus + producer surplus, and a monopoly usually reduces consumer surplus.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – उपभोक्ता जो भुगतान करने को तैयार है (-) जो वह वास्तव में भुगतान करता है</b><br>उपभोक्ता अधिशेष किसी वस्तु हेतु <b>उपभोक्ता की भुगतान करने की इच्छा वाली कीमत</b> तथा <b>वास्तव में चुकाई गई कीमत</b> का अंतर है। यह उपभोक्ता को क्रय से प्राप्त अतिरिक्त संतुष्टि या कल्याण मापता है और मांग वक्र के नीचे तथा बाजार कीमत के ऊपर के क्षेत्रफल से दर्शाया जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह संकल्पना <b>अल्फ्रेड मार्शल</b> ने दी; उपभोक्ता अधिशेष = कुल उपयोगिता − (कीमत × मात्रा)।<br>• मांग वक्र अधिकतम भुगतान-इच्छा दर्शाता है, अतः कीमत रेखा के ऊपर व मांग वक्र के नीचे का क्षेत्र उपभोक्ता अधिशेष होता है।<br>• <b>उत्पादक अधिशेष</b> विक्रेता को मिली कीमत तथा उस न्यूनतम कीमत का अंतर है जिस पर वह बेचने को तैयार होता है।<br>• पूर्ण प्रतिस्पर्धी बाजार में कुल कल्याण = उपभोक्ता अधिशेष + उत्पादक अधिशेष, तथा एकाधिकार सामान्यतः उपभोक्ता अधिशेष घटा देता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000074307","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: National Income","question":{"en":"What is the formula for net investment? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"शुद्ध निवेश का सूत्र क्या है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Gross investment - taxes","hi":"सकल निवेश - कर"},"2":{"en":"Gross investment - interest expense","hi":"सकल निवेश - ब्याज व्यय"},"3":{"en":"Gross investment - depreciation","hi":"सकल निवेश - ह्रास"},"4":{"en":"Gross investment - dividend","hi":"सकल निवेश - लाभांश"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Gross investment - depreciation</b><br>Net investment = Gross investment − Depreciation. Depreciation is the fall in the value of fixed capital due to wear and tear, so net investment shows the actual addition to the capital stock of an economy.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Gross investment includes replacement investment plus new addition to capital; net investment is the capital formation after making good the losses of depreciation.<br>• <b>Net National Product (NNP) = GNP − Depreciation</b>; NNP at factor cost is called <b>National Income</b>.<br>• Net domestic capital formation = Gross domestic capital formation − depreciation; it is a key indicator of economic growth.<br>• Gross investment is also called \"gross capital formation\" and includes fixed capital formation, inventories and valuables.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – सकल निवेश - ह्रास</b><br>शुद्ध निवेश = सकल निवेश − ह्रास (Depreciation)। ह्रास स्थायी पूँजी के मूल्य में घिसाव व प्रयोग के कारण होने वाली कमी है, अतः शुद्ध निवेश अर्थव्यवस्था की पूँजी स्टॉक में वास्तविक वृद्धि दर्शाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सकल निवेश में प्रतिस्थापन निवेश तथा पूँजी में नई वृद्धि दोनों सम्मिलित हैं; ह्रास की भरपाई के बाद की पूँजी निर्माण ही शुद्ध निवेश है।<br>• <b>शुद्ध राष्ट्रीय उत्पाद (NNP) = GNP − ह्रास</b>; साधन लागत पर NNP को <b>राष्ट्रीय आय</b> कहा जाता है।<br>• शुद्ध घरेलू पूँजी निर्माण = सकल घरेलू पूँजी निर्माण − ह्रास; यह आर्थिक वृद्धि का प्रमुख संकेतक है।<br>• सकल निवेश को \"सकल पूँजी निर्माण\" भी कहा जाता है, जिसमें स्थायी पूँजी निर्माण, स्टॉक तथा मूल्यवान वस्तुएँ सम्मिलित होती हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000074308","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: International News","question":{"en":"When was the QUAD (Quadrilateral Security Dialogue) revitalized? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"क्वाड (चतुर्पक्षीय सुरक्षा संवाद) का पुनर्जीवन कब हुआ? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2007"},"2":{"en":"2012"},"3":{"en":"2017"},"4":{"en":"2020"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 2017</b><br>The Quadrilateral Security Dialogue (QUAD), comprising India, the USA, Japan and Australia, was revived in <b>2017</b> after a gap of about a decade. Senior officials of the four countries met in Manila in November 2017, and the grouping was later upgraded to the foreign minister and summit levels.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Quad was first formed in <b>2007</b> when the four countries joined for the Malabar exercises and after the tsunami relief cooperation.<br>• Its focus areas are a free and open Indo-Pacific, maritime security, connectivity, cyber security, critical technology, health and climate.<br>• The first in-person Quad Leaders’ Summit was held at <b>Washington D.C. in 2021</b>; the 2024 summit was hosted by the USA at Wilmington, Delaware.<br>• The <b>Malabar</b> naval exercise is conducted by the Quad navies; India hosts it in rotation.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 2017</b><br>भारत, अमेरिका, जापान तथा ऑस्ट्रेलिया वाले चतुर्पक्षीय सुरक्षा संवाद (QUAD) का पुनर्जीवन लगभग एक दशक के अंतराल के बाद <b>2017</b> में हुआ। चारों देशों के वरिष्ठ अधिकारियों की बैठक नवंबर 2017 में मनीला में हुई और बाद में इस समूह को विदेश मंत्री तथा शिखर स्तर तक बढ़ाया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• क्वाड का पहला गठन <b>2007</b> में हुआ, जब चारों देश मलाबार अभ्यास तथा सुनामी राहत सहयोग के बाद एक साथ आए।<br>• इसके केंद्रीय विषय हैं — स्वतंत्र व खुला हिंद-प्रशांत, समुद्री सुरक्षा, संपर्क, साइबर सुरक्षा, महत्वपूर्ण प्रौद्योगिकी, स्वास्थ्य तथा जलवायु।<br>• पहला प्रत्यक्ष क्वाड नेताओं का शिखर सम्मेलन 2021 में वाशिंगटन डी.सी. में हुआ; 2024 का शिखर सम्मेलन अमेरिका ने विलमिंगटन, डेलावेयर में आयोजित किया।<br>• <b>मलाबार</b> नौसैन्य अभ्यास क्वाड देशों की नौसेनाओं द्वारा किया जाता है तथा भारत बारी-बारी से इसकी मेजबानी करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000074309","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"How many frames are there in a standard ten-pin bowling game? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मानक टेन-पिन बॉलिंग खेल में कितने फ्रेम होते हैं? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8"},"2":{"en":"9"},"3":{"en":"10"},"4":{"en":"11"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 10</b><br>A standard ten-pin bowling game has <b>10 frames</b>. In each frame a player gets two rolls to knock down all ten pins, and a bonus roll is allowed in the tenth frame for a strike or a spare.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• A <b>strike</b> means all ten pins are knocked down with the first ball and a <b>spare</b> means all pins are down with two balls.<br>• A perfect game — 12 strikes in a row — scores <b>300</b>, the maximum possible score.<br>• Ten-pin bowling is governed internationally by the <b>International Bowling Federation</b>; a lane is about 18.3 m long.<br>• The game originated in the USA in the 19th century and is now popular in the Commonwealth and Asian Games circuits.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 10</b><br>मानक टेन-पिन बॉलिंग खेल में <b>10 फ्रेम</b> होते हैं। प्रत्येक फ्रेम में खिलाड़ी को सभी दस पिन गिराने हेतु दो गेंदें मिलती हैं तथा दसवें फ्रेम में स्ट्राइक या स्पेयर पर अतिरिक्त गेंद मिलती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>स्ट्राइक</b> का अर्थ है पहली गेंद से ही सभी दस पिन गिरा देना तथा <b>स्पेयर</b> का अर्थ है दो गेंदों में सभी पिन गिराना।<br>• पूर्ण खेल — लगातार 12 स्ट्राइक — का स्कोर <b>300</b> होता है, जो अधिकतम संभव स्कोर है।<br>• टेन-पिन बॉलिंग का अंतर्राष्ट्रीय संचालन अंतर्राष्ट्रीय बॉलिंग महासंघ करता है; एक लेन लगभग 18.3 मीटर लंबी होती है।<br>• यह खेल 19वीं शताब्दी में अमेरिका में शुरू हुआ और अब राष्ट्रमंडल व एशियाई खेलों में लोकप्रिय है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000074310","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"During which year were the National Shooting Championships held in Trivandrum, Kerala? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"केरल के तिरुवनंतपुरम में राष्ट्रीय निशानेबाजी चैंपियनशिप किस वर्ष आयोजित हुई थी? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2013"},"2":{"en":"2019"},"3":{"en":"2022"},"4":{"en":"2020"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 2022</b><br>The rifle events of the <b>65th National Shooting Championship Competitions (NSCC)</b> were held at the Vattiyoorkkavu Shooting Range, Thiruvananthapuram (Trivandrum), Kerala from <b>20 November to 9 December 2022</b>, while the pistol events were held at Bhopal.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The championships are organised by the <b>National Rifle Association of India (NRAI)</b>, founded in 1951, which is affiliated to the ISSF.<br>• In 2022, <b>Manu Bhaker</b> won four gold medals in the women’s 25 m pistol events at the championships.<br>• Shooting is India’s most productive Olympic sport; <b>Abhinav Bindra</b> won India’s first individual Olympic gold in the 10 m air rifle at Beijing 2008.<br>• India’s shooting range for major events is the Karni Singh Shooting Range, New Delhi, named after the former NRAI president.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 2022</b><br><b>65वीं राष्ट्रीय निशानेबाजी चैंपियनशिप (NSCC)</b> की राइफल स्पर्धाएँ 20 नवंबर से 9 दिसंबर 2022 तक वट्टियूरकावु निशानेबाजी रेंज, तिरुवनंतपुरम, केरल में तथा पिस्टल स्पर्धाएँ भोपाल में हुईं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह चैंपियनशिप भारतीय राष्ट्रीय राइफल संघ (NRAI) आयोजित करता है, जिसकी स्थापना 1951 में हुई और जो ISSF से संबद्ध है।<br>• 2022 में <b>मनु भाकर</b> ने महिलाओं की 25 मीटर पिस्टल स्पर्धाओं में चार स्वर्ण पदक जीते।<br>• निशानेबाजी भारत का सर्वाधिक ओलंपिक पदक देने वाला खेल है; <b>अभिनव बिंद्रा</b> ने बीजिंग 2008 में 10 मीटर एयर राइफल में भारत का पहला व्यक्तिगत ओलंपिक स्वर्ण जीता।<br>• प्रमुख आयोजनों का भारतीय निशानेबाजी रेंज करनी सिंह शूटिंग रेंज, नई दिल्ली है, जिसका नाम NRAI के पूर्व अध्यक्ष के नाम पर है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000074311","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Who won India’s first Olympic medal in boxing? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मुक्केबाजी में भारत का पहला ओलंपिक पदक किसने जीता? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mary Kom","hi":"मैरी कॉम"},"2":{"en":"Vijender Singh","hi":"विजेंदर सिंह"},"3":{"en":"Shiva Thapa","hi":"शिवा थापा"},"4":{"en":"Lovlina Borgohain","hi":"लवलीना बोरगोहेन"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Vijender Singh</b><br><b>Vijender Singh</b> won the bronze medal in the middleweight (75 kg) category at the <b>Beijing Olympics 2008</b>, which was India’s first-ever Olympic medal in boxing.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Vijender Singh, from Bhiwani in Haryana, also won a bronze at the 2006 Asian Games and gold at the 2010 Asian Games.<br>• <b>Mary Kom</b> won bronze at London 2012 and is a six-time world champion; Lovlina Borgohain won bronze at Tokyo 2020.<br>• Boxing is governed in India by the <b>Boxing Federation of India</b> and internationally by the IBA; a bout has three rounds of three minutes.<br>• India’s other Olympic boxing medallists are Vijender Singh (2008), Mary Kom (2012), Lovlina Borgohain (2020) and Aman Sehrawat is a wrestling medallist, not boxing.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – विजेंदर सिंह</b><br><b>विजेंदर सिंह</b> ने <b>बीजिंग ओलंपिक 2008</b> में मिडलवेट (75 किग्रा) वर्ग में कांस्य पदक जीता, जो मुक्केबाजी में भारत का पहला ओलंपिक पदक था।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• हरियाणा के भिवानी से संबंधित विजेंदर सिंह ने 2006 एशियाई खेलों में कांस्य तथा 2010 एशियाई खेलों में स्वर्ण पदक भी जीता।<br>• <b>मैरी कॉम</b> ने लंदन 2012 में कांस्य जीता और वे छह बार विश्व चैंपियन रही हैं; लवलीना बोरगोहेन ने टोक्यो 2020 में कांस्य जीता।<br>• भारत में मुक्केबाजी का संचालन बॉक्सिंग फेडरेशन ऑफ इंडिया तथा अंतर्राष्ट्रीय स्तर पर IBA करता है; एक बाउट तीन राउंड की तीन मिनट की होती है।<br>• भारत के अन्य ओलंपिक मुक्केबाजी पदक विजेता विजेंदर सिंह (2008), मैरी कॉम (2012) तथा लवलीना बोरगोहेन (2020) हैं; अमन सेहरावत कुश्ती के पदक विजेता हैं, मुक्केबाजी के नहीं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000074312","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: National Organisations","question":{"en":"Which Home Affairs Minister has also been the 1<sup>st</sup> Minister of Co-operation since July 2021? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-से गृह मंत्री जुलाई 2021 से प्रथम सहकारिता मंत्री भी रहे हैं? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Amit Shah","hi":"अमित शाह"},"2":{"en":"J.P. Nadda","hi":"जे.पी. नड्डा"},"3":{"en":"Nitin Gadkari","hi":"नितिन गडकरी"},"4":{"en":"Rajnath Singh","hi":"राजनाथ सिंह"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Amit Shah</b><br><b>Amit Shah</b> is the Union Home Minister and became the <b>first Minister of Co-operation</b> when the new ministry was created on <b>6 July 2021</b>, to strengthen the co-operative movement in the country.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Ministry of Co-operation was carved out of the Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers’ Welfare and works on a \"Sahkar se Samriddhi\" approach.<br>• <b>Amit Shah</b> is a former BJP national president and was the Home Minister in 2019 and again from 2024.<br>• The nodal body for co-operatives is the <b>National Co-operative Development Corporation (NCDC)</b>, and the sector is governed by the Multi-State Co-operative Societies Act, 2002.<br>• <b>Rajnath Singh</b> was the Home Minister from 2014 to 2019, J.P. Nadda is the Health Minister and BJP president, and Nitin Gadkari heads the Road Transport and Highways Ministry.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – अमित शाह</b><br><b>अमित शाह</b> केंद्रीय गृह मंत्री हैं तथा देश में सहकारी आंदोलन को सुदृढ़ करने हेतु 6 जुलाई 2021 को गठित नए मंत्रालय के रूप में <b>प्रथम सहकारिता मंत्री</b> बने।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सहकारिता मंत्रालय को कृषि एवं किसान कल्याण मंत्रालय से अलग करके बनाया गया और यह \"सहकार से समृद्धि\" दृष्टिकोण पर कार्य करता है।<br>• <b>अमित शाह</b> भाजपा के पूर्व राष्ट्रीय अध्यक्ष हैं तथा 2019 और 2024 से गृह मंत्री हैं।<br>• सहकारी समितियों की नोडल संस्था राष्ट्रीय सहकारी विकास निगम (NCDC) है तथा यह क्षेत्र बहु-राज्यीय सहकारी समिति अधिनियम, 2002 से नियंत्रित होता है।<br>• <b>राजनाथ सिंह</b> 2014 से 2019 तक गृह मंत्री रहे, जे.पी. नड्डा स्वास्थ्य मंत्री व भाजपा अध्यक्ष हैं तथा नितिन गडकरी सड़क परिवहन एवं राजमार्ग मंत्रालय का नेतृत्व करते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000074313","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Mahajanapadas","question":{"en":"What was the capital of Avanti in the 6th century B.C? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"छठी शताब्दी ईसा पूर्व में अवंति की राजधानी क्या थी? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Taxila","hi":"तक्षशिला"},"2":{"en":"Pataliputra","hi":"पाटलिपुत्र"},"3":{"en":"Ayodhya","hi":"अयोध्या"},"4":{"en":"Ujjain","hi":"उज्जैन"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Ujjain</b><br>In the 6th century BCE, <b>Avanti</b> was one of the sixteen Mahajanapadas and its capital was <b>Ujjain (Ujjayini)</b>, on the river Shipra. Its other important city was Mahishmati.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The sixteen Mahajanapadas are mentioned in the <b>Anguttara Nikaya</b> and the Bhagavati Sutra; Avanti was one of the four most powerful, along with Magadha, Kosala and Vatsa.<br>• Avanti was finally annexed by <b>Magadha</b> under Chandragupta Maurya; Ujjain later became an important city of the Mauryan and Gupta empires.<br>• Other capitals: Magadha — Rajgriha and later Pataliputra; Kosala — Sravasti; Vatsa — Kaushambi; Gandhara — Taxila.<br>• <b>Pataliputra</b> (modern Patna) was the capital of Magadha and remained the capital of the Mauryas and Guptas.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – उज्जैन</b><br>छठी शताब्दी ईसा पूर्व में <b>अवंति</b> सोलह महाजनपदों में से एक था और इसकी राजधानी शिप्रा नदी के तट पर <b>उज्जैन (उज्जयिनी)</b> थी। इसका अन्य महत्वपूर्ण नगर माहिष्मती था।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सोलह महाजनपदों का उल्लेख <b>अंगुत्तर निकाय</b> तथा भगवती सूत्र में मिलता है; अवंति, मगध, कोसल व वत्स के साथ चार सर्वाधिक शक्तिशाली महाजनपदों में था।<br>• अवंति को अंततः चंद्रगुप्त मौर्य के अधीन <b>मगध</b> ने मिला लिया; बाद में उज्जैन मौर्य व गुप्त साम्राज्यों का महत्वपूर्ण नगर बना।<br>• अन्य राजधानियाँ: मगध — राजगृह व बाद में पाटलिपुत्र; कोसल — श्रावस्ती; वत्स — कौशांबी; गांधार — तक्षशिला।<br>• <b>पाटलिपुत्र</b> (आधुनिक पटना) मगध की राजधानी थी और मौर्य व गुप्त काल में भी राजधानी बनी रही।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000074314","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Peninsular Rivers","question":{"en":"Consider the following statements:<br><br>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Hamsaladeevi is located at the mouth of the Krishna River.<br><br>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Allahabad is located to the west of Varanasi.<br><br>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The Tons River is the largest tributary of the Yamuna River.<br><br>Which of the above statements is/are CORRECT? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित कथनों पर विचार कीजिए:<br><br>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;हंसलादेवी कृष्णा नदी के मुहाने पर स्थित है।<br><br>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;इलाहाबाद वाराणसी के पश्चिम में स्थित है।<br><br>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;टोंस नदी यमुना नदी की सबसे बड़ी सहायक नदी है।<br><br>उपर्युक्त कथनों में से कौन-सा/से सही है/हैं? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 and 2 only","hi":"केवल 1 और 2"},"2":{"en":"3 only","hi":"केवल 3"},"3":{"en":"2 only","hi":"केवल 2"},"4":{"en":"1, 2, and 3","hi":"1, 2 और 3"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – 1, 2, and 3</b><br>Hamsaladeevi lies at the mouth of the Krishna river in Krishna district of Andhra Pradesh; Allahabad (Prayagraj) is west of Varanasi on the Ganga; and the <b>Tons</b>, rising in the Har-ki-Dun glacier, is the largest tributary of the Yamuna. All three statements are correct.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Krishna rises near Mahabaleshwar in Maharashtra and falls into the Bay of Bengal near Hamsaladeevi, forming a delta with the Godavari.<br>• The <b>Tons</b> joins the Yamuna near Dehradun and carries the largest volume of water among the Yamuna’s tributaries; other tributaries are the Chambal, Betwa, Ken and Sind.<br>• Prayagraj is at the confluence (Triveni) of the Ganga, Yamuna and the mythical Saraswati, and the Kumbh Mela is held here.<br>• The Yamuna rises from the Yamunotri glacier and is the longest tributary of the Ganga, joining it at Prayagraj.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – 1, 2 और 3</b><br>हंसलादेवी आंध्र प्रदेश के कृष्णा जिले में कृष्णा नदी के मुहाने पर स्थित है; इलाहाबाद (प्रयागराज) गंगा पर वाराणसी के पश्चिम में है; तथा हर-की-दून हिमनद से निकलने वाली <b>टोंस</b> यमुना की सबसे बड़ी सहायक नदी है। अतः तीनों कथन सही हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• कृष्णा महाराष्ट्र में महाबलेश्वर के निकट से निकलती है और हंसलादेवी के निकट बंगाल की खाड़ी में गिरती है, जहाँ गोदावरी के साथ संयुक्त डेल्टा बनाती है।<br>• <b>टोंस</b> देहरादून के निकट यमुना में मिलती है और यमुना की सहायक नदियों में सर्वाधिक जल लाती है; अन्य सहायक नदियाँ चंबल, बेतवा, केन व सिंध हैं।<br>• प्रयागराज गंगा, यमुना तथा पौराणिक सरस्वती के संगम (त्रिवेणी) पर स्थित है और यहाँ कुंभ मेला लगता है।<br>• यमुना यमुनोत्री हिमनद से निकलती है और गंगा की सबसे लंबी सहायक नदी है, जो प्रयागराज में गंगा में मिलती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000074315","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"Which traditional Naga folk song is specifically known as a war song, narrating themes of bravery and battle? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-सा पारंपरिक नागा लोकगीत विशेष रूप से युद्ध गीत के रूप में जाना जाता है, जिसमें वीरता और युद्ध के विषय वर्णित होते हैं? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Neuleu","hi":"न्यूल्यू"},"2":{"en":"Heliamleu","hi":"हेलियामल्यू"},"3":{"en":"Jemji","hi":"जेमजी"},"4":{"en":"Tati","hi":"ताती"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Heliamleu</b><br><b>Heliamleu</b> is a traditional Naga folk song sung as a <b>war song</b>, narrating tales of bravery and battle. It belongs to the Zeliangrong community of Nagaland and is sung while recounting the heroic deeds of warriors.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Naga folk music is largely vocal and community-based; the <b>Zeliangrong</b> comprise the Zeme, Liangmai and Rongmei tribes.<br>• Other Naga folk songs include <b>Neuleu</b>, <b>Jemji</b> and <b>Tati</b>, sung during festivals, harvests and social ceremonies.<br>• The Hornbill Festival, held every December at <b>Kisama</b> near Kohima, showcases Naga dance, music and crafts.<br>• Nagaland is home to 17 major tribes, and its traditional festivals include Sekrenyi (Angami), Moatsu (Ao), Aoleang (Konyak) and Tuluni (Sumi).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – हेलियामल्यू</b><br><b>हेलियामल्यू</b> एक पारंपरिक नागा लोकगीत है जो <b>युद्ध गीत</b> के रूप में गाया जाता है और वीरता तथा युद्ध की कथाएँ वर्णित करता है। यह नागालैंड के ज़ेलियांगरोंग समुदाय से संबंधित है तथा योद्धाओं के पराक्रम का बखान करते हुए गाया जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• नागा लोकसंगीत मुख्यतः स्वर-प्रधान एवं सामुदायिक है; <b>ज़ेलियांगरोंग</b> में ज़ेमे, लियांगमाई व रोंगमेई जनजातियाँ सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• अन्य नागा लोकगीतों में <b>न्यूल्यू</b>, <b>जेमजी</b> तथा <b>ताती</b> सम्मिलित हैं, जो उत्सवों, फसल कटाई तथा सामाजिक समारोहों में गाए जाते हैं।<br>• कोहिमा के निकट <b>किसामा</b> में प्रतिवर्ष दिसंबर में हॉर्नबिल महोत्सव आयोजित होता है, जिसमें नागा नृत्य, संगीत व शिल्प प्रदर्शित होते हैं।<br>• नागालैंड में 17 प्रमुख जनजातियाँ हैं; प्रमुख पारंपरिक उत्सवों में सेकरेन्यी (अंगामी), मोआत्सु (आओ), आओलेंग (कोन्याक) तथा तुलुनी (सुमी) सम्मिलित हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000074316","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Indus Valley Civilization","question":{"en":"What was the primary purpose of the saddle querns discovered at Harappan sites? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"हड़प्पा स्थलों से प्राप्त सैडल क्वॉर्न (चक्की) का प्राथमिक उद्देश्य क्या था? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"For making sharp weapons","hi":"तेज शस्त्र बनाने हेतु"},"2":{"en":"For grinding daily cereals","hi":"दैनिक अनाज पीसने हेतु"},"3":{"en":"For building tall houses","hi":"ऊँचे मकान बनाने हेतु"},"4":{"en":"For digging deep rivers","hi":"गहरी नदियाँ खोदने हेतु"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – For grinding daily cereals</b><br><b>Saddle querns</b> are flat, saddle-shaped stone slabs used with a stone pestle or muller for <b>grinding daily cereals</b> such as wheat and barley. They were household tools found in Harappan kitchens and granary areas.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The saddle quern and the muller are typical <b>Neolithic to Harappan</b> grinding stones; the later \"rotary quern\" came into use in the early historic period.<br>• Harappans grew <b>wheat, barley, rice, peas, sesame and cotton</b> and stored grain in granaries, as at Harappa and Mohenjodaro.<br>• Other Harappan tools included copper–bronze sickles, chisels, arrowheads, fish hooks and weights of chert in multiples of 16.<br>• Important evidence of food habits comes from charred grain, querns, grinding stones and animal bones at sites such as Lothal, Kalibangan and Banawali.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – दैनिक अनाज पीसने हेतु</b><br><b>सैडल क्वॉर्न</b> सपाट, काठी (saddle) के आकार की पत्थर की पट्टियाँ होती थीं, जिनका उपयोग पत्थर के मूसल के साथ गेहूँ व जौ जैसे <b>दैनिक अनाज पीसने</b> हेतु होता था। ये हड़प्पा के घरों व अन्नागार क्षेत्रों में मिलने वाले घरेलू उपकरण थे।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सैडल क्वॉर्न व मूसल <b>नवपाषाण से हड़प्पा</b> काल के विशिष्ट पेषण पत्थर हैं; बाद में \"घूमने वाली चक्की\" (rotary quern) प्रचलित हुई।<br>• हड़प्पावासी <b>गेहूँ, जौ, चावल, मटर, तिल व कपास</b> उगाते थे तथा हड़प्पा व मोहनजोदड़ो जैसे स्थलों के अन्नागारों में अनाज संग्रह करते थे।<br>• अन्य हड़प्पा उपकरणों में तांबे-कांसे की हँसिया, छेनी, बाणाग्र, मछली के काँटे तथा 16 के गुणकों में चर्ट के बाट सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• लोथल, कालीबंगा व बनावली जैसे स्थलों से जले अनाज, चक्की, पेषण पत्थर तथा पशु अस्थियों से खाद्य आदतों के प्रमाण मिलते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000074317","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Constitutional and Non-Constitutional Bodies","question":{"en":"According to Article 76(1) of the Indian Constitution, a person appointed as Attorney-General for India must be qualified to be appointed as a: [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान के अनुच्छेद 76(1) के अनुसार, भारत के महान्यायवादी के रूप में नियुक्त व्यक्ति को किस रूप में नियुक्त होने की योग्यता रखनी चाहिए? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"District Judge","hi":"जिला न्यायाधीश"},"2":{"en":"High Court Judge","hi":"उच्च न्यायालय न्यायाधीश"},"3":{"en":"Supreme Court Judge","hi":"सर्वोच्च न्यायालय न्यायाधीश"},"4":{"en":"Member of Parliament","hi":"संसद सदस्य"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Supreme Court Judge</b><br>Article 76(1) provides that the Attorney-General of India is appointed by the President and must be a person <b>qualified to be appointed as a judge of the Supreme Court</b>. He is the first law officer of the Government of India.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Attorney-General is appointed by the <b>President</b>, holds office during his pleasure and is not a full-time government servant; he can take private legal practice.<br>• He has the right to speak and take part in the proceedings of both Houses of Parliament and its committees but cannot vote.<br>• Article 76 also provides for a <b>Solicitor-General of India</b>, the second law officer, whose office is not given the same constitutional detail.<br>• A person qualifies for appointment as a Supreme Court judge if he has been a High Court judge for five years, or an advocate of a High Court for ten years, or a distinguished jurist (Article 124).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – सर्वोच्च न्यायालय न्यायाधीश</b><br>अनुच्छेद 76(1) में प्रावधान है कि भारत का महान्यायवादी राष्ट्रपति द्वारा नियुक्त किया जाता है और वह ऐसा व्यक्ति होना चाहिए जो <b>सर्वोच्च न्यायालय का न्यायाधीश नियुक्त होने की योग्यता</b> रखता हो। वह भारत सरकार का प्रथम विधि अधिकारी होता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• महान्यायवादी की नियुक्ति <b>राष्ट्रपति</b> करता है, वह राष्ट्रपति के प्रसादपर्यंत पद पर रहता है, पूर्णकालिक सरकारी सेवक नहीं होता तथा निजी विधिक पेशा भी कर सकता है।<br>• उसे संसद के दोनों सदनों व उनकी समितियों की कार्यवाही में बोलने व भाग लेने का अधिकार है, परंतु मत देने का नहीं।<br>• अनुच्छेद 76 में <b>भारत के सॉलिसिटर-जनरल</b> का भी प्रावधान है, जो द्वितीय विधि अधिकारी है।<br>• सर्वोच्च न्यायालय के न्यायाधीश हेतु कोई व्यक्ति तब योग्य माना जाता है जब वह पाँच वर्ष उच्च न्यायालय का न्यायाधीश, दस वर्ष उच्च न्यायालय का अधिवक्ता या विशिष्ट विधिवेत्ता हो (अनुच्छेद 124)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000074318","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Minerals","question":{"en":"Naharkatiya, known for oil production, is located in which state? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"तेल उत्पादन हेतु प्रसिद्ध नहरकटिया किस राज्य में स्थित है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Gujarat","hi":"गुजरात"},"2":{"en":"Rajasthan","hi":"राजस्थान"},"3":{"en":"Meghalaya","hi":"मेघालय"},"4":{"en":"Assam","hi":"असम"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Assam</b><br>Naharkatiya (Naharkatia) is an oil field in the <b>Dibrugarh district of Assam</b>, about 32 km south-west of Digboi on the Burhi Dihing river. Oil was discovered there in 1953 and production began in 1954.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Digboi</b> in Assam is the birthplace of India’s oil industry; the first oil well was dug in 1866 and the Digboi refinery was commissioned in 1901.<br>• Naharkatiya crude is supplied to the refineries at <b>Noonmati (Guwahati)</b> and Barauni (Bihar) through pipelines.<br>• Other Assam oil fields are Moran, Rudrasagar, Geleki and Lakwa; Assam is India’s oldest oil-producing state.<br>• Major oil fields of India include <b>Mumbai High</b> (offshore), Ankleshwar and Kalol (Gujarat), Barmer (Rajasthan) and Krishna–Godavari basin (Andhra Pradesh).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – असम</b><br>नहरकटिया <b>असम के डिब्रूगढ़ जिले</b> में बुरही दिहिंग नदी पर डिबगोई से लगभग 32 किमी दक्षिण-पश्चिम में स्थित तेल क्षेत्र है। यहाँ 1953 में तेल की खोज हुई और 1954 में उत्पादन आरंभ हुआ।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• असम का <b>डिबगोई</b> भारत के तेल उद्योग का जन्मस्थान है; पहला तेल कुआँ 1866 में खोदा गया तथा डिबगोई रिफाइनरी 1901 में स्थापित हुई।<br>• नहरकटिया का कच्चा तेल पाइपलाइन द्वारा <b>नूनमाटी (गुवाहाटी)</b> तथा बरौनी (बिहार) की रिफाइनरियों को भेजा जाता है।<br>• असम के अन्य तेल क्षेत्र मोरान, रुद्रसागर, गेलेकी व लखवा हैं; असम भारत का सबसे पुराना तेल उत्पादक राज्य है।<br>• भारत के प्रमुख तेल क्षेत्रों में <b>मुंबई हाई</b> (तटवर्ती), अंकलेश्वर व कलोल (गुजरात), बाड़मेर (राजस्थान) तथा कृष्णा–गोदावरी बेसिन (आंध्र प्रदेश) सम्मिलित हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000074319","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Transport","question":{"en":"Identify the <b>correct</b> stretch covered under National Waterway 3 (NW-3) in India. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत में राष्ट्रीय जलमार्ग 3 (NW-3) के अंतर्गत आने वाले <b>सही</b> विस्तार को पहचानिए। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Prayagraj–Haldia stretch","hi":"प्रयागराज–हल्दिया विस्तार"},"2":{"en":"Sadiya–Dhubri stretch","hi":"सदिया–धुबरी विस्तार"},"3":{"en":"Kottapuram–Kollam stretch","hi":"कोट्टापुरम–कोल्लम विस्तार"},"4":{"en":"Kottapuram–Dhubri stretch","hi":"कोट्टापुरम–धुबरी विस्तार"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Kottapuram–Kollam stretch</b><br>National Waterway 3 (NW-3), the <b>West Coast Canal</b>, runs from <b>Kottapuram to Kollam</b> in Kerala, covering about 205 km, and includes the Champakara and Udyogamandal canals. It is one of the busiest and most developed waterways in India.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>NW-1</b>: Ganga–Bhagirathi–Hooghly from Prayagraj to Haldia (about 1,620 km).<br>• <b>NW-2</b>: Brahmaputra from Sadiya to Dhubri (about 891 km).<br>• <b>NW-4</b>: Godavari–Krishna river system in Andhra Pradesh and Telangana; <b>NW-5</b>: Brahmani–Mahanadi delta with the East Coast Canal in Odisha.<br>• The <b>Inland Waterways Authority of India (IWAI)</b>, set up in 1986 at Noida, develops and regulates national waterways.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – कोट्टापुरम–कोल्लम विस्तार</b><br>राष्ट्रीय जलमार्ग 3 (NW-3), अर्थात् <b>पश्चिमी तट नहर</b>, केरल में <b>कोट्टापुरम से कोल्लम</b> तक लगभग 205 किमी में विस्तृत है तथा इसमें चंपाकारा व उद्योगमंडल नहरें सम्मिलित हैं। यह भारत के सर्वाधिक व्यस्त व विकसित जलमार्गों में से एक है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>NW-1</b>: प्रयागराज से हल्दिया तक गंगा–भागीरथी–हुगली (लगभग 1,620 किमी)।<br>• <b>NW-2</b>: सदिया से धुबरी तक ब्रह्मपुत्र (लगभग 891 किमी)।<br>• <b>NW-4</b>: आंध्र प्रदेश व तेलंगाना में गोदावरी–कृष्णा नदी प्रणाली; <b>NW-5</b>: ओडिशा में ब्राह्मणी–महानदी डेल्टा तथा पूर्वी तट नहर।<br>• भारतीय अंतर्देशीय जलमार्ग प्राधिकरण (IWAI), जिसकी स्थापना 1986 में नोएडा में हुई, राष्ट्रीय जलमार्गों का विकास व नियमन करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000074320","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"In which sport did Karnam Malleswari win India’s first-ever Olympic medal by a woman at the 2000 Sydney Olympic Games? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"2000 के सिडनी ओलंपिक खेलों में कर्नम मल्लेश्वरी ने किस खेल में भारत का महिला द्वारा जीता गया पहला ओलंपिक पदक जीता? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Boxing","hi":"मुक्केबाजी"},"2":{"en":"Weightlifting","hi":"भारोत्तोलन"},"3":{"en":"Wrestling","hi":"कुश्ती"},"4":{"en":"Shooting","hi":"निशानेबाजी"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Weightlifting</b><br>Karnam Malleswari won the <b>bronze medal in weightlifting</b> (69 kg category) at the Sydney Olympics in 2000, becoming the first Indian woman to win an Olympic medal.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Malleswari, from Voosavanipeta in Andhra Pradesh, also won gold at the 1994 and 1995 World Weightlifting Championships.<br>• She was awarded the <b>Padma Shri (1999)</b> and the Rajiv Gandhi Khel Ratna (1995) and later joined the Indian Railways.<br>• Weightlifting has two lifts in competition — the <b>snatch</b> and the <b>clean and jerk</b> — and the total of both decides the winner.<br>• Other Indian Olympic medallists in weightlifting: <b>Karnam Malleswari (2000)</b> and <b>Mirabai Chanu</b>, who won silver in the 49 kg category at Tokyo 2020.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – भारोत्तोलन</b><br>कर्नम मल्लेश्वरी ने 2000 के सिडनी ओलंपिक में <b>भारोत्तोलन</b> (69 किग्रा वर्ग) में कांस्य पदक जीतकर ओलंपिक पदक जीतने वाली पहली भारतीय महिला बनीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• आंध्र प्रदेश के वूसवानीपेटा की मल्लेश्वरी ने 1994 व 1995 की विश्व भारोत्तोलन चैंपियनशिप में स्वर्ण पदक भी जीता।<br>• उन्हें <b>पद्म श्री (1999)</b> तथा राजीव गांधी खेल रत्न (1995) से सम्मानित किया गया; बाद में वे भारतीय रेल में शामिल हुईं।<br>• भारोत्तोलन प्रतियोगिता में दो भार उठाए जाते हैं — <b>स्नैच</b> तथा <b>क्लीन एंड जर्क</b> — और दोनों का कुल भार विजेता तय करता है।<br>• भारोत्तोलन के अन्य भारतीय ओलंपिक पदक विजेता <b>कर्नम मल्लेश्वरी (2000)</b> तथा <b>मीराबाई चानू</b> हैं, जिन्होंने टोक्यो 2020 में 49 किग्रा वर्ग में रजत जीता।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000074321","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Northern Plains and Islands","question":{"en":"The highest peak of the Nicobar group is: [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निकोबार समूह का सर्वोच्च शिखर है: [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mount Thullier","hi":"माउंट थुलियर"},"2":{"en":"Mount Diavolo","hi":"माउंट डायवोलो"},"3":{"en":"Saddle Peak","hi":"सैडल पीक"},"4":{"en":"Mount Koyob","hi":"माउंट कोयोब"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Mount Thullier</b><br><b>Mount Thullier</b> (642 m), on Great Nicobar Island, is the highest peak of the Nicobar group of islands. The Andaman group, by contrast, has Saddle Peak as its highest point.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Saddle Peak</b> (732 m) on North Andaman is the highest peak of the entire Andaman and Nicobar Islands.<br>• The Nicobar group lies south of the Ten Degree Channel and includes Car Nicobar, Great Nicobar, Little Nicobar and the Nancowry group.<br>• The <b>Ten Degree Channel</b> separates the Andaman and Nicobar groups, and the <b>Nine Degree Channel</b> separates Minicoy from the Lakshadweep islands.<br>• <b>Indira Point</b> on Great Nicobar is the southernmost point of India; the Andaman and Nicobar Islands are the largest archipelago of the country.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – माउंट थुलियर</b><br>ग्रेट निकोबार द्वीप पर स्थित <b>माउंट थुलियर</b> (642 मीटर) निकोबार द्वीप समूह का सर्वोच्च शिखर है। इसके विपरीत अंडमान समूह का सर्वोच्च बिंदु सैडल पीक है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• उत्तर अंडमान का <b>सैडल पीक</b> (732 मीटर) संपूर्ण अंडमान-निकोबार द्वीप समूह का सर्वोच्च शिखर है।<br>• निकोबार समूह दस डिग्री चैनल के दक्षिण में है, जिसमें कार निकोबार, ग्रेट निकोबार, लिटिल निकोबार तथा नानकौरी समूह सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• <b>दस डिग्री चैनल</b> अंडमान व निकोबार समूह को अलग करता है, तथा <b>नौ डिग्री चैनल</b> मिनिकॉय को लक्षद्वीप से पृथक करता है।<br>• ग्रेट निकोबार पर <b>इंदिरा पॉइंट</b> भारत का दक्षिणतम बिंदु है; अंडमान-निकोबार देश का सबसे बड़ा द्वीपसमूह है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000074322","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Centre-State Relations","question":{"en":"In India, which Article of the Constitution empowers Parliament to exclude the jurisdiction of the Supreme Court in matters relating to inter-State water disputes? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत में, संविधान का कौन-सा अनुच्छेद संसद को अंतर-राज्यीय जल विवादों से संबंधित विषयों में सर्वोच्च न्यायालय के अधिकारक्षेत्र को बाहर करने की शक्ति देता है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Article 262","hi":"अनुच्छेद 262"},"2":{"en":"Article 263","hi":"अनुच्छेद 263"},"3":{"en":"Article 356","hi":"अनुच्छेद 356"},"4":{"en":"Article 131","hi":"अनुच्छेद 131"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Article 262</b><br><b>Article 262</b> provides that Parliament may by law provide for the adjudication of any dispute relating to the waters of an inter-State river or river valley, and may by law exclude the jurisdiction of the Supreme Court and other courts in such disputes.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Parliament used this power to enact the <b>Inter-State River Water Disputes Act, 1956</b>, under which tribunals such as the Cauvery, Krishna and Ravi-Beas tribunals were set up.<br>• <b>Article 263</b> provides for an Inter-State Council to inquire into and advise on disputes between states.<br>• <b>Article 131</b> gives the Supreme Court original jurisdiction in disputes between the Centre and states, and <b>Article 356</b> deals with President’s Rule in a state.<br>• Water is a subject in the <b>State List</b> (Entry 17), but inter-state rivers are in the Union List (Entry 56), which leads to conflicts such as the Cauvery dispute.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – अनुच्छेद 262</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 262</b> में प्रावधान है कि संसद विधि द्वारा अंतर-राज्यीय नदी या नदी घाटी के जल से संबंधित विवाद के न्यायनिर्णयन का उपबंध कर सकती है तथा ऐसे विवादों में सर्वोच्च न्यायालय व अन्य न्यायालयों के अधिकारक्षेत्र को बाहर कर सकती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• संसद ने इस शक्ति का प्रयोग करते हुए <b>अंतर-राज्यीय नदी जल विवाद अधिनियम, 1956</b> बनाया, जिसके अंतर्गत कावेरी, कृष्णा तथा रावी-ब्यास जैसे अधिकरण गठित हुए।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 263</b> राज्यों के बीच विवादों की जाँच व सलाह हेतु अंतर-राज्य परिषद का प्रावधान करता है।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 131</b> केंद्र-राज्य विवादों में सर्वोच्च न्यायालय को प्रारंभिक अधिकारक्षेत्र देता है, तथा <b>अनुच्छेद 356</b> राज्य में राष्ट्रपति शासन से संबंधित है।<br>• जल <b>राज्य सूची</b> (प्रविष्टि 17) का विषय है, परंतु अंतर-राज्यीय नदियाँ संघ सूची (प्रविष्टि 56) में हैं, जिससे कावेरी विवाद जैसे संघर्ष उत्पन्न होते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000074323","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: National Parks","question":{"en":"Consider the following statements about Shekha Jheel Bird Sanctuary:<br>1. It is located in the Aligarh district of Uttar Pradesh.<br>2. It was designated as Uttar Pradesh’s 12th Ramsar site and India’s 99th Ramsar site in April 2026.<br>Which of the statements given above is/are <b>correct</b>? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"शेखा झील पक्षी अभयारण्य के संबंध में निम्नलिखित कथनों पर विचार कीजिए:<br>1. यह उत्तर प्रदेश के अलीगढ़ जिले में स्थित है।<br>2. इसे अप्रैल 2026 में उत्तर प्रदेश का 12वाँ रामसर स्थल तथा भारत का 99वाँ रामसर स्थल घोषित किया गया।<br>उपर्युक्त कथनों में से कौन-सा/से <b>सही</b> है/हैं? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only 1","hi":"केवल 1"},"2":{"en":"Only 2","hi":"केवल 2"},"3":{"en":"Both 1 and 2","hi":"1 और 2 दोनों"},"4":{"en":"Neither 1 nor 2","hi":"न 1, न ही 2"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Both 1 and 2</b><br>Shekha Jheel Bird Sanctuary lies in the <b>Aligarh district of Uttar Pradesh</b>, and on <b>22 April 2026</b> it was designated as India’s <b>99th Ramsar site</b> and Uttar Pradesh’s <b>12th Ramsar site</b>. Both statements are therefore correct.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Shekha Jheel is a freshwater perennial wetland of about 25 hectares, formed by the <b>Upper Ganga Canal (1852)</b>, and lies on the Central Asian Flyway.<br>• The Ramsar Convention on Wetlands was signed at <b>Ramsar, Iran, in 1971</b> and came into force in 1975; India joined it in 1982.<br>• India has 99 Ramsar sites, the highest in Asia; Tamil Nadu and Uttar Pradesh have the largest number of such sites.<br>• Other Ramsar sites of Uttar Pradesh include <b>Patna Bird Sanctuary (97th)</b> and Surha Tal (100th).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 1 और 2 दोनों</b><br>शेखा झील पक्षी अभयारण्य <b>उत्तर प्रदेश के अलीगढ़ जिले</b> में स्थित है तथा 22 अप्रैल 2026 को इसे भारत का <b>99वाँ रामसर स्थल</b> और उत्तर प्रदेश का <b>12वाँ रामसर स्थल</b> घोषित किया गया। अतः दोनों कथन सही हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• शेखा झील लगभग 25 हेक्टेयर का मीठे जल का बारहमासी आर्द्रभूमि क्षेत्र है, जो <b>ऊपरी गंगा नहर (1852)</b> से बना तथा मध्य एशियाई उड़ान मार्ग पर स्थित है।<br>• आर्द्रभूमि पर रामसर अभिसमय 1971 में रामसर, ईरान में हस्ताक्षरित तथा 1975 में प्रभावी हुआ; भारत 1982 में इसमें शामिल हुआ।<br>• भारत में 99 रामसर स्थल हैं, जो एशिया में सर्वाधिक हैं; तमिलनाडु व उत्तर प्रदेश में ऐसे स्थलों की संख्या सबसे अधिक है।<br>• उत्तर प्रदेश के अन्य रामसर स्थलों में <b>पटना पक्षी अभयारण्य (97वाँ)</b> तथा सुरहा ताल (100वाँ) सम्मिलित हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000074324","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Making of Constitution","question":{"en":"When did the British first accept, in principle, the demand for an Indian Constituent Assembly? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"ब्रिटिश सरकार ने भारतीय संविधान सभा की मांग को सैद्धांतिक रूप से सर्वप्रथम कब स्वीकार किया? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"August Offer (1940)","hi":"अगस्त प्रस्ताव (1940)"},"2":{"en":"Cripps Proposals (1942)","hi":"क्रिप्स प्रस्ताव (1942)"},"3":{"en":"Cabinet Mission (1946)","hi":"कैबिनेट मिशन (1946)"},"4":{"en":"Mountbatten Plan (1947)","hi":"माउंटबेटन योजना (1947)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – August Offer (1940)</b><br>The <b>August Offer of 1940</b>, made by Viceroy <b>Lord Linlithgow</b>, accepted for the first time, in principle, the demand for an Indian Constituent Assembly to frame the constitution, although with the right of minorities to have their views examined. The offer was rejected by the Congress.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Cripps Mission (1942)</b> went further and proposed a constitution-making body elected by the provincial assemblies.<br>• The <b>Cabinet Mission (1946)</b> put forward a concrete plan for a Constituent Assembly, which was set up in November 1946 and held its first meeting on <b>9 December 1946</b>.<br>• The Constituent Assembly adopted the Constitution on <b>26 November 1949</b> and it came into force on <b>26 January 1950</b>.<br>• Dr. Rajendra Prasad was the President of the Constituent Assembly, while <b>Dr. B.R. Ambedkar</b> chaired the Drafting Committee.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – अगस्त प्रस्ताव (1940)</b><br>वायसराय <b>लॉर्ड लिनलिथगो</b> के <b>अगस्त प्रस्ताव, 1940</b> ने सर्वप्रथम सैद्धांतिक रूप से संविधान निर्माण हेतु भारतीय संविधान सभा की माँग स्वीकार की, यद्यपि अल्पसंख्यकों के विचार परीक्षण के अधिकार के साथ। कांग्रेस ने इस प्रस्ताव को अस्वीकार कर दिया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>क्रिप्स मिशन (1942)</b> ने आगे बढ़कर प्रांतीय विधानसभाओं द्वारा निर्वाचित संविधान-निर्माण निकाय का प्रस्ताव रखा।<br>• <b>कैबिनेट मिशन (1946)</b> ने संविधान सभा हेतु ठोस योजना प्रस्तुत की; संविधान सभा नवंबर 1946 में गठित हुई तथा इसकी पहली बैठक <b>9 दिसंबर 1946</b> को हुई।<br>• संविधान सभा ने संविधान को <b>26 नवंबर 1949</b> को अपनाया तथा यह <b>26 जनवरी 1950</b> से लागू हुआ।<br>• संविधान सभा के अध्यक्ष डॉ. राजेंद्र प्रसाद थे, जबकि <b>डॉ. भीमराव आंबेडकर</b> प्रारूप समिति के अध्यक्ष थे।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000074325","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"As an outcome of the economic reforms initiated in 1991, which sector recorded the highest average annual growth rate during 2007–12? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"1991 में आरंभ किए गए आर्थिक सुधारों के परिणामस्वरूप, 2007–12 के दौरान किस क्षेत्र ने सर्वाधिक औसत वार्षिक वृद्धि दर दर्ज की? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Agriculture sector","hi":"कृषि क्षेत्र"},"2":{"en":"Industrial sector","hi":"औद्योगिक क्षेत्र"},"3":{"en":"Services sector","hi":"सेवा क्षेत्र"},"4":{"en":"Domestic sector","hi":"घरेलू क्षेत्र"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Services sector</b><br>After the 1991 reforms, the <b>services sector</b> became the fastest-growing and largest sector of the Indian economy, recording an average annual growth well above that of agriculture and industry during 2007–12 (the Eleventh Plan period).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Services contribute over <b>half of India’s GVA</b>, with trade, hotels, transport, communication, financial and real estate services as the main sub-sectors.<br>• In the Eleventh Plan (2007–12), services grew at around <b>9–9.5%</b>, industry at about 7% and agriculture at around 3% per year.<br>• The IT–BPM sector, telecommunications and banking grew fastest after liberalisation, and India became a global hub of software and business services.<br>• Growth in agriculture and industry is more volatile because of monsoon dependence and investment cycles, while services has grown steadily.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – सेवा क्षेत्र</b><br>1991 के सुधारों के बाद <b>सेवा क्षेत्र</b> भारतीय अर्थव्यवस्था का सर्वाधिक तेजी से बढ़ने वाला तथा सबसे बड़ा क्षेत्र बन गया, जिसने 2007–12 (ग्यारहवीं योजना अवधि) में कृषि व उद्योग की तुलना में कहीं अधिक औसत वार्षिक वृद्धि दर्ज की।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सेवा क्षेत्र भारत के <b>सकल मूल्य वर्धन (GVA) के आधे से अधिक</b> का योगदान देता है, जिसमें व्यापार, होटल, परिवहन, संचार, वित्तीय तथा रियल एस्टेट सेवाएँ प्रमुख हैं।<br>• ग्यारहवीं योजना (2007–12) में सेवा क्षेत्र लगभग <b>9–9.5%</b>, उद्योग लगभग 7% तथा कृषि लगभग 3% प्रति वर्ष बढ़ी।<br>• उदारीकरण के बाद आईटी–बीपीएम, दूरसंचार व बैंकिंग तेजी से बढ़े और भारत सॉफ्टवेयर व व्यावसायिक सेवाओं का वैश्विक केंद्र बना।<br>• कृषि व उद्योग की वृद्धि मानसून व निवेश चक्रों पर निर्भर होने से अधिक अस्थिर है, जबकि सेवा क्षेत्र लगातार बढ़ता रहा।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000074326","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Budget and Taxation","question":{"en":"One of the key objectives of the Chelliah Committee during the 1991 economic reforms was to make India’s taxation system: [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"1991 के आर्थिक सुधारों के दौरान चेलैया समिति का एक प्रमुख उद्देश्य भारत की कराधान प्रणाली को कैसा बनाना था? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Centralised and uniform","hi":"केंद्रीकृत और एकरूप"},"2":{"en":"Broad-based and fair","hi":"व्यापक आधारित और न्यायपूर्ण"},"3":{"en":"State-controlled only","hi":"केवल राज्य-नियंत्रित"},"4":{"en":"Export-oriented only","hi":"केवल निर्यात-उन्मुख"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Broad-based and fair</b><br>The <b>Chelliah Committee (1991–93)</b> on tax reforms recommended simplifying and rationalising the tax structure so as to make it <b>broad-based, equitable and fair</b>, with lower rates, fewer slabs and a wider tax net.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The committee was headed by <b>Dr. Raja J. Chelliah</b> and recommended moderate tax rates, minimal exemptions and better compliance.<br>• Its recommendations led to a fall in the maximum personal income tax rate and customs duty rates, and to the introduction of service tax in <b>1994</b>.<br>• Later reform committees include the <b>Kelkar Committee</b> on direct and indirect taxes, which led to the FRBM Act and the GST roadmap.<br>• The Goods and Services Tax came into force on <b>1 July 2017</b> as a \"one nation, one tax\" reform, replacing many indirect taxes.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – व्यापक आधारित और न्यायपूर्ण</b><br>कर सुधार हेतु <b>चेलैया समिति (1991–93)</b> ने कर ढाँचे को सरल व तर्कसंगत बनाकर उसे <b>व्यापक आधारित, समतापूर्ण व न्यायपूर्ण</b> बनाने की सिफारिश की, जिसमें कम दरें, कम स्लैब तथा विस्तृत कर दायरा हो।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• समिति के अध्यक्ष <b>डॉ. राजा जे. चेलैया</b> थे; इसने मध्यम कर दरें, न्यूनतम छूट तथा बेहतर अनुपालन की सिफारिश की।<br>• इसकी सिफारिशों से व्यक्तिगत आयकर की अधिकतम दर व सीमा शुल्क दरें घटीं तथा <b>1994</b> में सेवा कर लागू हुआ।<br>• बाद की सुधार समितियों में प्रत्यक्ष व अप्रत्यक्ष कर हेतु <b>केलकर समिति</b> सम्मिलित है, जिससे FRBM अधिनियम तथा GST की रूपरेखा बनी।<br>• वस्तु एवं सेवा कर (GST) <b>1 जुलाई 2017</b> से \"एक राष्ट्र, एक कर\" सुधार के रूप में लागू हुआ, जिसने अनेक अप्रत्यक्ष करों का स्थान लिया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000074327","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Census","question":{"en":"According to Census terminology, the “Houseless Population” includes persons who: [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"जनगणना शब्दावली के अनुसार, \"बेघर जनसंख्या\" में वे व्यक्ति सम्मिलित हैं जो: [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Live in rented houses","hi":"किराए के मकानों में रहते हैं"},"2":{"en":"Live in temporary shelters only","hi":"केवल अस्थायी आश्रयों में रहते हैं"},"3":{"en":"Live in government buildings","hi":"सरकारी भवनों में रहते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Do not live in census houses","hi":"जनगणना मकानों में नहीं रहते"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Do not live in census houses</b><br>In Census terminology, the <b>houseless population</b> consists of persons who do not live in census houses — that is, those found living in the open, on pavements, under flyovers, in railway stations, bus shelters, temples or other places not meant for living.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Census of India counts the population under two broad categories — <b>houseless population</b> and population living in <b>census houses</b> (with a roof and walls).<br>• The concept is used in the Houseless Population Schedule of the census to estimate urban homelessness and plan welfare schemes.<br>• India’s first census was conducted in <b>1872</b> under Lord Mayo, and the first synchronous census in <b>1881</b> under Lord Ripon; the census is held every <b>10 years</b>.<br>• Census 2011 was the <b>15th census</b> and the 7th after independence; it recorded a population of 121.09 crore and a literacy rate of 74.04%.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – जनगणना मकानों में नहीं रहते</b><br>जनगणना शब्दावली में <b>बेघर जनसंख्या (Houseless Population)</b> में वे व्यक्ति सम्मिलित हैं जो जनगणना मकानों में नहीं रहते — अर्थात् जो खुले में, फुटपाथों पर, फ्लाईओवर के नीचे, रेलवे स्टेशनों, बस शेल्टरों, मंदिरों या रहने योग्य नहीं ऐसे स्थानों पर पाए जाते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत की जनगणना जनसंख्या को दो बड़ी श्रेणियों में गिनती है — <b>बेघर जनसंख्या</b> तथा <b>जनगणना मकानों</b> (छत व दीवार सहित) में रहने वाली जनसंख्या।<br>• यह संकल्पना जनगणना की बेघर जनसंख्या अनुसूची में प्रयुक्त होकर शहरी बेघरता का अनुमान तथा कल्याण योजनाओं का नियोजन करती है।<br>• भारत की पहली जनगणना 1872 में लॉर्ड मेयो के समय हुई तथा पहली समकालिक जनगणना 1881 में लॉर्ड रिपन के समय; जनगणना प्रत्येक <b>10 वर्ष</b> में होती है।<br>• जनगणना 2011 <b>15वीं जनगणना</b> तथा स्वतंत्रता के बाद सातवीं थी; इसमें जनसंख्या 121.09 करोड़ तथा साक्षरता दर 74.04% दर्ज हुई।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000074328","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Vedic Age","question":{"en":"The earliest Indian literature is best described as which of the following? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"प्राचीनतम भारतीय साहित्य का सर्वोत्तम वर्णन निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Written","hi":"लिखित"},"2":{"en":"Printed","hi":"मुद्रित"},"3":{"en":"Oral","hi":"मौखिक"},"4":{"en":"Digital","hi":"डिजिटल"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Oral</b><br>The earliest Indian literature, the <b>Vedas</b>, was composed and preserved in <b>oral</b> form for centuries before it was written down. The hymns were transmitted from teacher to pupil through recitation, which is why Vedic literature is called <i>sruti</i> — \"that which is heard\".<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Rigveda was composed around <b>1500–1000 BCE</b> and passed on orally with remarkable accuracy through the <b>guru–shishya</b> tradition.<br>• Vedic literature is divided into the <b>Samhitas</b> (hymns), <b>Brahmanas</b> (rituals), <b>Aranyakas</b> (forest texts) and <b>Upanishads</b> (philosophy).<br>• Writing in India became common with the <b>Brahmi and Kharosthi</b> scripts in the Mauryan period, from the 3rd century BCE.<br>• Other early Indian texts include the Ramayana and Mahabharata, which too were preserved orally as epics before being written.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – मौखिक</b><br>प्राचीनतम भारतीय साहित्य <b>वेद</b> लिखे जाने से पहले सदियों तक <b>मौखिक</b> रूप में रचा व सुरक्षित रखा गया। मंत्र गुरु से शिष्य तक पाठ द्वारा पहुँचाए जाते थे, इसी कारण वैदिक साहित्य को <i>श्रुति</i> — \"जो सुना गया\" — कहा जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• ऋग्वेद की रचना लगभग 1500–1000 ईसा पूर्व हुई और यह <b>गुरु–शिष्य</b> परंपरा से अद्भुत शुद्धता के साथ मौखिक रूप में सुरक्षित रहा।<br>• वैदिक साहित्य <b>संहिताओं</b> (मंत्र), <b>ब्राह्मणों</b> (कर्मकांड), <b>आरण्यकों</b> (अरण्य ग्रंथ) तथा <b>उपनिषदों</b> (दर्शन) में विभाजित है।<br>• भारत में लेखन मौर्यकाल में तीसरी शताब्दी ईसा पूर्व से <b>ब्राह्मी व खरोष्ठी</b> लिपियों के साथ सामान्य हुआ।<br>• अन्य प्रारंभिक भारतीय ग्रंथों में रामायण व महाभारत सम्मिलित हैं, जो लिखे जाने से पहले महाकाव्यों के रूप में मौखिक रूप से सुरक्षित रहे।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000074329","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Five Year Plan and Industrial Policy Resolution","question":{"en":"Which sector was accorded the highest priority under the Second Five-Year Plan? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"द्वितीय पंचवर्षीय योजना में किस क्षेत्र को सर्वोच्च प्राथमिकता दी गई? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Heavy and basic industries","hi":"भारी और आधारभूत उद्योग"},"2":{"en":"Agriculture and irrigation","hi":"कृषि और सिंचाई"},"3":{"en":"Foreign trade promotion","hi":"विदेश व्यापार संवर्धन"},"4":{"en":"School education sector","hi":"विद्यालय शिक्षा क्षेत्र"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Heavy and basic industries</b><br>The Second Five-Year Plan (1956–61) gave the highest priority to the development of <b>heavy and basic industries</b> such as iron and steel, heavy machinery, chemicals and power. It was based on the <b>Mahalanobis model</b> of rapid industrialisation.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Second Plan is also called the <b>industrialisation plan</b>; it was linked to the Industrial Policy Resolution of 1956 and set up steel plants at Bhilai, Rourkela and Durgapur.<br>• Its target growth rate was 4.5% and the plan is credited with creating the capital goods base of India.<br>• The First Plan (1951–56) had given priority to <b>agriculture, irrigation and power</b> and was a success.<br>• The Second Plan’s heavy industry focus caused a shortage of consumer goods and food grains, and India faced a foreign exchange crisis by 1957 (the \"sterling crisis\").","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – भारी और आधारभूत उद्योग</b><br>द्वितीय पंचवर्षीय योजना (1956–61) में लौह-इस्पात, भारी मशीनरी, रसायन तथा विद्युत जैसे <b>भारी एवं आधारभूत उद्योगों</b> के विकास को सर्वोच्च प्राथमिकता दी गई। यह तीव्र औद्योगीकरण के <b>महालनोबिस मॉडल</b> पर आधारित थी।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• द्वितीय योजना को <b>औद्योगीकरण योजना</b> भी कहा जाता है; यह औद्योगिक नीति प्रस्ताव 1956 से जुड़ी थी और इसने भिलाई, राउरकेला व दुर्गापुर में इस्पात संयंत्र स्थापित किए।<br>• इसका वृद्धि लक्ष्य 4.5% था तथा इसे भारत में पूँजीगत वस्तु आधार बनाने का श्रेय मिलता है।<br>• प्रथम योजना (1951–56) ने <b>कृषि, सिंचाई व विद्युत</b> को प्राथमिकता दी थी और वह सफल रही।<br>• द्वितीय योजना के भारी उद्योग केंद्रित होने से उपभोक्ता वस्तुओं व खाद्यान्न की कमी हुई तथा 1957 तक भारत को विदेशी मुद्रा संकट (\"स्टर्लिंग संकट\") का सामना करना पड़ा।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000074330","section":"GK","topic":"Chemistry: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"In the moving boundary method used to determine an ion’s transport number, what is the primary purpose of adding an indicator electrolyte to the principal electrolyte? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किसी आयन की परिवहन संख्या (transport number) निर्धारित करने में प्रयुक्त गतिशील सीमा विधि (moving boundary method) में मुख्य विद्युत-अपघट्य में संकेतक विद्युत-अपघट्य (indicator electrolyte) मिलाने का प्राथमिक उद्देश्य क्या है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To increase the conductivity of the solution","hi":"विलयन की चालकता बढ़ाना"},"2":{"en":"To ensure complete dissociation of the principal electrolyte","hi":"मुख्य विद्युत-अपघट्य का पूर्ण वियोजन सुनिश्चित करना"},"3":{"en":"To form a sharp and visible boundary for measuring ion migration","hi":"आयन विस्थापन मापने हेतु तीक्ष्ण तथा दृश्यमान सीमा बनाना"},"4":{"en":"To prevent current flow through the cell","hi":"सेल में धारा प्रवाह रोकना"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – To form a sharp and visible boundary for measuring ion migration</b><br>In the moving boundary method, an <b>indicator electrolyte</b> is added to create a well-defined, visible boundary (for example with a coloured ion or a change of refractive index). The movement of this <b>sharp boundary</b> under the applied current is measured to calculate the transport number of the ion.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Transport number (Hittorf number) = the fraction of total current carried by a particular ion; the sum of the transport numbers of cation and anion is 1.<br>• The indicator electrolyte must have a <b>common ion</b> with the principal electrolyte and a lower mobility than the leading ion for a stable boundary.<br>• Transport numbers are determined by the <b>Hittorf method</b> and the moving boundary method; in the Hittorf method concentration changes near the electrodes are measured.<br>• The transport number varies with concentration and reaches its limiting value at infinite dilution; it is related to ionic mobility by \\(t_+ = \\frac{u_+}{u_+ + u_-}\\).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – आयन विस्थापन मापने हेतु तीक्ष्ण तथा दृश्यमान सीमा बनाना</b><br>गतिशील सीमा विधि में सुस्पष्ट व दृश्यमान सीमा बनाने हेतु <b>संकेतक विद्युत-अपघट्य</b> मिलाया जाता है (जैसे रंगीन आयन अथवा अपवर्तनांक में परिवर्तन द्वारा)। लगाई गई धारा के अंतर्गत इस <b>तीक्ष्ण सीमा</b> की गति मापकर आयन की परिवहन संख्या की गणना की जाती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• परिवहन संख्या (हिटॉर्फ संख्या) = किसी विशिष्ट आयन द्वारा वहन की गई कुल धारा का भाग; धनायन व ऋणायन की परिवहन संख्याओं का योग 1 होता है।<br>• स्थायी सीमा हेतु संकेतक विद्युत-अपघट्य में मुख्य विद्युत-अपघट्य के साथ <b>उभयनिष्ठ आयन</b> होना तथा उसकी गतिशीलता अग्रणी आयन से कम होनी चाहिए।<br>• परिवहन संख्या <b>हिटॉर्फ विधि</b> तथा गतिशील सीमा विधि द्वारा निर्धारित होती है; हिटॉर्फ विधि में इलेक्ट्रोडों के निकट सांद्रता परिवर्तन मापा जाता है।<br>• परिवहन संख्या सांद्रता के साथ बदलती है और अनंत तनुता पर सीमांत मान प्राप्त करती है; यह आयनिक गतिशीलता से \\(t_+ = \\frac{u_+}{u_+ + u_-}\\) द्वारा संबंधित है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000074331","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"If the volume of a right prism is 150 cm³ and the height is 5 cm, its base area is: [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि एक लंब प्रिज्म का आयतन 150 cm³ है और ऊँचाई 5 cm है, तो इसके आधार का क्षेत्रफल है: [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"35 cm²"},"2":{"en":"45 cm²"},"3":{"en":"30 cm²"},"4":{"en":"50 cm²"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"175\" height=\"145\" viewBox=\"0 0 175 145\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M20 45H100V120H20ZM20 45L50 20H130L100 45M130 20V95L100 120\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M50 20V95H130M50 95L20 120\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"138\" y=\"72\">h = 5</text></g></svg><br>Volume of prism = Base area × Height<br>\\(150 = \\text{Base area} \\times 5\\)<br>Base area = \\(\\frac{150}{5} = \\boxed{30}\\) cm²<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 30 cm².</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"175\" height=\"145\" viewBox=\"0 0 175 145\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M20 45H100V120H20ZM20 45L50 20H130L100 45M130 20V95L100 120\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M50 20V95H130M50 95L20 120\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"138\" y=\"72\">h = 5</text></g></svg><br>प्रिज्म का आयतन = आधार का क्षेत्रफल × ऊँचाई<br>\\(150 = \\text{Base area} \\times 5\\)<br>आधार का क्षेत्रफल = \\(\\frac{150}{5} = \\boxed{30}\\) cm²<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 30 cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000074332","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"A scalene triangle has sides in the ratio 13:14:15. If its perimeter is 126 cm, find the length of its longest side. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक विषमबाहु त्रिभुज की भुजाएँ 13:14:15 के अनुपात में हैं। यदि इसका परिमाप 126 cm है, तो इसकी सबसे लंबी भुजा की लंबाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"52 cm"},"2":{"en":"48 cm"},"3":{"en":"42 cm"},"4":{"en":"45 cm"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"196\" height=\"152\" viewBox=\"0 0 196 152\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M75 18L30 126H156Z\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"75\" y=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"130\">B</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"130\">C</text><text x=\"93\" y=\"142\" text-anchor=\"middle\">14k</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"72\">15k</text><text x=\"46\" y=\"72\" text-anchor=\"end\">13k</text></g></svg><br>Sides = 13k, 14k, 15k<br>\\(13k + 14k + 15k = 126 \\Rightarrow 42k = 126 \\Rightarrow k = 3\\)<br>Longest side = \\(15 \\times 3 = \\boxed{45}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 45 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"196\" height=\"152\" viewBox=\"0 0 196 152\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M75 18L30 126H156Z\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"75\" y=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"130\">B</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"130\">C</text><text x=\"93\" y=\"142\" text-anchor=\"middle\">14k</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"72\">15k</text><text x=\"46\" y=\"72\" text-anchor=\"end\">13k</text></g></svg><br>भुजाएँ = 13k, 14k, 15k<br>\\(13k + 14k + 15k = 126 \\Rightarrow 42k = 126 \\Rightarrow k = 3\\)<br>सबसे लंबी भुजा = \\(15 \\times 3 = \\boxed{45}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 45 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000074333","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"Calculate the volume of a cylinder whose circular base area measures 154 cm² and whose height is 20 cm. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"उस बेलन का आयतन ज्ञात कीजिए जिसके वृत्तीय आधार का क्षेत्रफल 154 cm² है और जिसकी ऊँचाई 20 cm है। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3080 cm³"},"2":{"en":"2580 cm³"},"3":{"en":"2480 cm³"},"4":{"en":"2180 cm³"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"170\" height=\"140\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 140\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><ellipse cx=\"70\" cy=\"22\" rx=\"50\" ry=\"12\"/><path d=\"M20 22V112M120 22V112M20 112a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 112a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 22H120M70 22V112\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"31\">r</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"72\">h = 20</text></g></svg><br>Volume = Base area × Height<br>\\(= 154 \\times 20 = \\boxed{3080}\\) cm³<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 3080 cm³.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"170\" height=\"140\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 140\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><ellipse cx=\"70\" cy=\"22\" rx=\"50\" ry=\"12\"/><path d=\"M20 22V112M120 22V112M20 112a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 112a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 22H120M70 22V112\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"31\">r</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"72\">h = 20</text></g></svg><br>आयतन = आधार का क्षेत्रफल × ऊँचाई<br>\\(= 154 \\times 20 = \\boxed{3080}\\) cm³<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 3080 cm³ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000074334","section":"MATH","topic":"Partnership","question":{"en":"X and Y start a business with capital in the ratio 5 : 6. At the end of 8 months, X withdraws his capital. If they receive profits in the ratio 5 : 9, for how long was Y's capital used in the business? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"X और Y 5 : 6 के अनुपात में पूँजी लगाकर एक व्यवसाय शुरू करते हैं। 8 महीने के अंत में, X अपनी पूँजी निकाल लेता है। यदि उन्हें 5 : 9 के अनुपात में लाभ मिलता है, तो Y की पूँजी व्यवसाय में कितने समय तक लगी रही? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"10 months","hi":"10 महीने"},"2":{"en":"12 months","hi":"12 महीने"},"3":{"en":"14 months","hi":"14 महीने"},"4":{"en":"15 months","hi":"15 महीने"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Profit ratio = Capital × Time<br>X : Y = \\(5 \\times 8 : 6 \\times t = 40 : 6t\\)<br>\\(\\frac{40}{6t} = \\frac{5}{9} \\Rightarrow 30t = 360\\)<br>\\(t = \\boxed{12}\\) months<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 12 months.</b>","hi":"लाभ का अनुपात = पूँजी × समय<br>X : Y = \\(5 \\times 8 : 6 \\times t = 40 : 6t\\)<br>\\(\\frac{40}{6t} = \\frac{5}{9} \\Rightarrow 30t = 360\\)<br>\\(t = \\boxed{12}\\) महीने<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 12 महीने है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000074335","section":"MATH","topic":"Average","question":{"en":"Given that the average of five numbers is 27, and that excluding one number reduces the average to 25, determine the value of the excluded number. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिया गया है कि पाँच संख्याओं का औसत 27 है, और एक संख्या को हटाने पर औसत घटकर 25 हो जाता है, तो हटाई गई संख्या का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"45"},"2":{"en":"35"},"3":{"en":"55"},"4":{"en":"65"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Sum of 5 numbers = \\(5 \\times 27 = 135\\)<br>Sum of remaining 4 numbers = \\(4 \\times 25 = 100\\)<br>Excluded number = \\(135 - 100 = \\boxed{35}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 35.</b>","hi":"5 संख्याओं का योग = \\(5 \\times 27 = 135\\)<br>शेष 4 संख्याओं का योग = \\(4 \\times 25 = 100\\)<br>हटाई गई संख्या = \\(135 - 100 = \\boxed{35}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 35 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000074336","section":"MATH","topic":"Compound Interest (CI)","question":{"en":"Calculate the compound interest on ₹12,000 at 10% per annum for 1 year 6 months, compounded annually. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"₹12,000 पर 10% वार्षिक दर से 1 वर्ष 6 महीने के लिए चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज ज्ञात कीजिए, जब ब्याज वार्षिक रूप से संयोजित होता है। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹1460"},"2":{"en":"₹1860"},"3":{"en":"₹1560"},"4":{"en":"₹1660"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Interest for 1st year = 10% of 12000 = ₹1200 → Amount = ₹13200<br>For the next 6 months, rate = \\(\\frac{10}{2} = 5\\%\\)<br>Interest = 5% of 13200 = ₹660<br>CI = \\(1200 + 660 = \\boxed{1860}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): ₹1860.</b>","hi":"पहले वर्ष का ब्याज = 12000 का 10% = ₹1200 → मिश्रधन = ₹13200<br>अगले 6 महीनों के लिए दर = \\(\\frac{10}{2} = 5\\%\\)<br>ब्याज = 13200 का 5% = ₹660<br>चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज = \\(1200 + 660 = \\boxed{1860}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ₹1860 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000074337","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"If the ratio of the number of sides of two regular polygons is 5:4 and the difference between their interior angles is 9°. Find the number of sides of the polygon with more sides. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि दो सम बहुभुजों की भुजाओं की संख्या का अनुपात 5:4 है और उनके आंतरिक कोणों का अंतर 9° है, तो अधिक भुजाओं वाले बहुभुज की भुजाओं की संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4"},"2":{"en":"10"},"3":{"en":"8"},"4":{"en":"15"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Let sides = 5k and 4k. Interior angle = \\(180^\\circ - \\frac{360^\\circ}{n}\\)<br>Difference = \\(\\frac{360}{4k} - \\frac{360}{5k} = \\frac{90}{k} - \\frac{72}{k} = \\frac{18}{k}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{18}{k} = 9 \\Rightarrow k = 2\\)<br>Sides of larger polygon = \\(5 \\times 2 = \\boxed{10}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 10.</b>","hi":"माना भुजाएँ = 5k और 4k. आंतरिक कोण = \\(180^\\circ - \\frac{360^\\circ}{n}\\)<br>अंतर = \\(\\frac{360}{4k} - \\frac{360}{5k} = \\frac{90}{k} - \\frac{72}{k} = \\frac{18}{k}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{18}{k} = 9 \\Rightarrow k = 2\\)<br>बड़े बहुभुज की भुजाएँ = \\(5 \\times 2 = \\boxed{10}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 10 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000074338","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"The ratio of the radii of two concentric circles is 5: 3. If the difference between their areas is 256π sq. m, what is the radius of the smaller circle? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दो संकेंद्रीय वृत्तों की त्रिज्याओं का अनुपात 5: 3 है। यदि उनके क्षेत्रफलों का अंतर 256π वर्ग मीटर है, तो छोटे वृत्त की त्रिज्या क्या है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"20 m"},"2":{"en":"10 m"},"3":{"en":"16 m"},"4":{"en":"12 m"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"160\" height=\"150\" viewBox=\"0 0 160 150\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"75\" r=\"60\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"75\" r=\"34\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"75\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M80 75H140M80 75L56 51\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"119\" y=\"70\">5k</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"72\" text-anchor=\"end\">3k</text></g></svg><br>Difference of areas = \\(\\pi[(5k)^2 - (3k)^2] = 16\\pi k^2\\)<br>\\(16\\pi k^2 = 256\\pi \\Rightarrow k^2 = 16 \\Rightarrow k = 4\\)<br>Smaller radius = \\(3 \\times 4 = \\boxed{12}\\) m<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 12 m.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"160\" height=\"150\" viewBox=\"0 0 160 150\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"75\" r=\"60\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"75\" r=\"34\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"75\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M80 75H140M80 75L56 51\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"119\" y=\"70\">5k</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"72\" text-anchor=\"end\">3k</text></g></svg><br>क्षेत्रफलों का अंतर = \\(\\pi[(5k)^2 - (3k)^2] = 16\\pi k^2\\)<br>\\(16\\pi k^2 = 256\\pi \\Rightarrow k^2 = 16 \\Rightarrow k = 4\\)<br>छोटी त्रिज्या = \\(3 \\times 4 = \\boxed{12}\\) m<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 12 m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000074339","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"The height of a right circular cone is 15 cm and its slant height is 17 cm. Find the curved surface area of the cone. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक लंब वृत्तीय शंकु की ऊँचाई 15 cm है और इसकी तिर्यक ऊँचाई 17 cm है। शंकु का वक्र पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"149π cm²"},"2":{"en":"120π cm²"},"3":{"en":"136π cm²"},"4":{"en":"125π cm²"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"170\" height=\"135\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 135\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M70 15L20 110M70 15L120 110M20 110a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 110a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 15V110M70 110H120\"/><path d=\"M70 100h8v10\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"96\" y=\"106\">r</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"72\">15</text><text x=\"102\" y=\"56\">17</text></g></svg><br>\\(r = \\sqrt{17^2 - 15^2} = \\sqrt{64} = 8\\) cm<br>CSA = \\(\\pi r l = \\pi \\times 8 \\times 17 = \\boxed{136\\pi}\\) cm²<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 136π cm².</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"170\" height=\"135\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 135\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M70 15L20 110M70 15L120 110M20 110a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 110a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 15V110M70 110H120\"/><path d=\"M70 100h8v10\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"96\" y=\"106\">r</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"72\">15</text><text x=\"102\" y=\"56\">17</text></g></svg><br>\\(r = \\sqrt{17^2 - 15^2} = \\sqrt{64} = 8\\) cm<br>वक्र पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल = \\(\\pi r l = \\pi \\times 8 \\times 17 = \\boxed{136\\pi}\\) cm²<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 136π cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000074340","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"A ladder of length 20 m makes an angle of 60° with the ground. Find the distance of the foot from the wall. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"20 m लंबी एक सीढ़ी जमीन के साथ 60° का कोण बनाती है। सीढ़ी के पाद की दीवार से दूरी ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8 m"},"2":{"en":"13 m"},"3":{"en":"10 m"},"4":{"en":"12 m"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"137\" height=\"165\" viewBox=\"0 0 137 165\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M22 141H92V20Z\"/><path d=\"M83 141v-9h9\"/><path d=\"M44 141A22 22 0 0 0 33 122\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"8\" y=\"155\">A</text><text x=\"94\" y=\"155\">B</text><text x=\"96\" y=\"24\">C</text><text x=\"48\" y=\"136\">60°</text><text x=\"57\" y=\"156\" text-anchor=\"middle\">x</text><text x=\"49\" y=\"75\" text-anchor=\"end\">20 m</text></g></svg><br>AC = ladder = 20 m, BC = wall, AB = x<br>\\(\\cos 60^\\circ = \\frac{x}{20}\\)<br>\\(x = 20 \\times \\frac{1}{2} = \\boxed{10}\\) m<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 10 m.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"137\" height=\"165\" viewBox=\"0 0 137 165\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M22 141H92V20Z\"/><path d=\"M83 141v-9h9\"/><path d=\"M44 141A22 22 0 0 0 33 122\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"8\" y=\"155\">A</text><text x=\"94\" y=\"155\">B</text><text x=\"96\" y=\"24\">C</text><text x=\"48\" y=\"136\">60°</text><text x=\"57\" y=\"156\" text-anchor=\"middle\">x</text><text x=\"49\" y=\"75\" text-anchor=\"end\">20 m</text></g></svg><br>AC = सीढ़ी = 20 m, BC = दीवार, AB = x<br>\\(\\cos 60^\\circ = \\frac{x}{20}\\)<br>\\(x = 20 \\times \\frac{1}{2} = \\boxed{10}\\) m<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 10 m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000074341","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"CD is a chord of a circle and E lies on the minor arc CD. Tangents at C and D meet at F. If \\(\\angle CED = 118^\\circ\\), find \\(\\angle CFD\\). [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"CD एक वृत्त की जीवा है और E लघु चाप CD पर स्थित है। C और D पर खींची गई स्पर्श रेखाएँ F पर मिलती हैं। यदि \\(\\angle CED = 118^\\circ\\) है, तो \\(\\angle CFD\\) ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"45°"},"2":{"en":"56°"},"3":{"en":"68°"},"4":{"en":"75°"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"184\" height=\"242\" viewBox=\"0 0 184 242\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M36 115L92 26L148 115M41 118L44 113L39 110M143 118L139 113L144 110M36 115L92 84L148 115M83 89A10 10 0 0 0 101 89M85 36A12 12 0 0 0 98 36\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M92 150L36 115M92 150L148 115\"/><circle cx=\"92\" cy=\"150\" r=\"66\"/><circle cx=\"92\" cy=\"150\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"92\" y=\"166\">O</text><text x=\"23\" y=\"112\">C</text><text x=\"161\" y=\"112\">D</text><text x=\"92\" y=\"23\">F</text><text x=\"92\" y=\"81\">E</text><text x=\"92\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"11\">118°</text><text x=\"92\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"11\">?</text></g></svg><br>E is on the minor arc, so \\(\\angle CED\\) stands on the major arc.<br>Major arc CD = \\(2 \\times 118^\\circ = 236^\\circ\\) → Minor arc CD = \\(360^\\circ - 236^\\circ = 124^\\circ\\)<br>Angle between tangents = \\(180^\\circ - \\text{minor arc}\\)<br>\\(\\angle CFD = 180^\\circ - 124^\\circ = \\boxed{56^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 56°.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"184\" height=\"242\" viewBox=\"0 0 184 242\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M36 115L92 26L148 115M41 118L44 113L39 110M143 118L139 113L144 110M36 115L92 84L148 115M83 89A10 10 0 0 0 101 89M85 36A12 12 0 0 0 98 36\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M92 150L36 115M92 150L148 115\"/><circle cx=\"92\" cy=\"150\" r=\"66\"/><circle cx=\"92\" cy=\"150\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"92\" y=\"166\">O</text><text x=\"23\" y=\"112\">C</text><text x=\"161\" y=\"112\">D</text><text x=\"92\" y=\"23\">F</text><text x=\"92\" y=\"81\">E</text><text x=\"92\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"11\">118°</text><text x=\"92\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"11\">?</text></g></svg><br>E लघु चाप पर है, अतः \\(\\angle CED\\) दीर्घ चाप पर बनता है।<br>दीर्घ चाप CD = \\(2 \\times 118^\\circ = 236^\\circ\\) → लघु चाप CD = \\(360^\\circ - 236^\\circ = 124^\\circ\\)<br>स्पर्श रेखाओं के बीच का कोण = \\(180^\\circ - \\text{minor arc}\\)<br>\\(\\angle CFD = 180^\\circ - 124^\\circ = \\boxed{56^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 56° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000074342","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If \\(\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta - \\cot\\theta = p\\), find the value of \\(\\frac{p^2 - 1}{p^2 + 1}\\). [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta - \\cot\\theta = p\\) है, तो \\(\\frac{p^2 - 1}{p^2 + 1}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\cos\\theta\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\sin\\theta\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(-\\cos\\theta\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(-\\sin\\theta\\)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(p = \\frac{1 - \\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta} \\Rightarrow p^2 = \\frac{(1 - \\cos\\theta)^2}{1 - \\cos^2\\theta} = \\frac{1 - \\cos\\theta}{1 + \\cos\\theta}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{p^2 - 1}{p^2 + 1} = \\frac{(1 - \\cos\\theta) - (1 + \\cos\\theta)}{(1 - \\cos\\theta) + (1 + \\cos\\theta)} = \\frac{-2\\cos\\theta}{2}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{-\\cos\\theta}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): \\(-\\cos\\theta\\).</b>","hi":"\\(p = \\frac{1 - \\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta} \\Rightarrow p^2 = \\frac{(1 - \\cos\\theta)^2}{1 - \\cos^2\\theta} = \\frac{1 - \\cos\\theta}{1 + \\cos\\theta}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{p^2 - 1}{p^2 + 1} = \\frac{(1 - \\cos\\theta) - (1 + \\cos\\theta)}{(1 - \\cos\\theta) + (1 + \\cos\\theta)} = \\frac{-2\\cos\\theta}{2}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{-\\cos\\theta}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): \\(-\\cos\\theta\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000074343","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(x = 7 + 4\\sqrt{3}\\), what is the value of \\(\\left(\\sqrt{x} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\right)^2\\)? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(x = 7 + 4\\sqrt{3}\\) है, तो \\(\\left(\\sqrt{x} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\right)^2\\) का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"10"},"2":{"en":"11"},"3":{"en":"12"},"4":{"en":"14"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(x = 7 + 4\\sqrt{3} = (2 + \\sqrt{3})^2 \\Rightarrow \\sqrt{x} = 2 + \\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}} = 2 - \\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(\\sqrt{x} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}} = 2\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\((2\\sqrt{3})^2 = \\boxed{12}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 12.</b>","hi":"\\(x = 7 + 4\\sqrt{3} = (2 + \\sqrt{3})^2 \\Rightarrow \\sqrt{x} = 2 + \\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}} = 2 - \\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(\\sqrt{x} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}} = 2\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\((2\\sqrt{3})^2 = \\boxed{12}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 12 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000074344","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(x = \\sqrt{\\frac{7 + 4\\sqrt{3}}{7 - 4\\sqrt{3}}}\\), then what is the value of \\(x^2 - 14x + 2\\)? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(x = \\sqrt{\\frac{7 + 4\\sqrt{3}}{7 - 4\\sqrt{3}}}\\) है, तो \\(x^2 - 14x + 2\\) का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0"},"2":{"en":"1"},"3":{"en":"2"},"4":{"en":"3"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(x = \\sqrt{\\frac{(2 + \\sqrt{3})^2}{(2 - \\sqrt{3})^2}} = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{3}}{2 - \\sqrt{3}} = (2 + \\sqrt{3})^2 = 7 + 4\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{x} = 7 - 4\\sqrt{3} \\Rightarrow x + \\frac{1}{x} = 14\\)<br>\\(x^2 + 1 = 14x \\Rightarrow x^2 - 14x + 1 = 0\\)<br>\\(x^2 - 14x + 2 = 0 + 1 = \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 1.</b>","hi":"\\(x = \\sqrt{\\frac{(2 + \\sqrt{3})^2}{(2 - \\sqrt{3})^2}} = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{3}}{2 - \\sqrt{3}} = (2 + \\sqrt{3})^2 = 7 + 4\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{x} = 7 - 4\\sqrt{3} \\Rightarrow x + \\frac{1}{x} = 14\\)<br>\\(x^2 + 1 = 14x \\Rightarrow x^2 - 14x + 1 = 0\\)<br>\\(x^2 - 14x + 2 = 0 + 1 = \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000074345","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"The radius of a sphere is increased by 50%. By what percentage does its volume increase? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक गोले की त्रिज्या में 50% की वृद्धि की जाती है। इसके आयतन में कितने प्रतिशत की वृद्धि होती है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"154.5%"},"2":{"en":"165.5%"},"3":{"en":"237.5%"},"4":{"en":"254.5%"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"135\" height=\"125\" viewBox=\"0 0 135 125\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"65\" r=\"50\"/><path d=\"M15 65a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M15 65a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M65 65H115\"/><circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"65\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"61\">r</text></g></svg><br>Volume ∝ r³. New radius = \\(\\frac{3}{2}\\) times<br>New volume = \\(\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^3 = \\frac{27}{8}\\) times<br>Increase = \\(\\frac{27 - 8}{8} \\times 100 = \\boxed{237.5\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 237.5%.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"135\" height=\"125\" viewBox=\"0 0 135 125\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"65\" r=\"50\"/><path d=\"M15 65a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M15 65a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M65 65H115\"/><circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"65\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"61\">r</text></g></svg><br>आयतन ∝ r³. नई त्रिज्या = \\(\\frac{3}{2}\\) गुना<br>नया आयतन = \\(\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^3 = \\frac{27}{8}\\) गुना<br>वृद्धि = \\(\\frac{27 - 8}{8} \\times 100 = \\boxed{237.5\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 237.5% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000074346","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In triangle ABC, DE is parallel to BC, AD = x + 1, DB = 2x, AE = 3x + 2, EC = 5x. Find the value of x (x &gt; 0). [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"त्रिभुज ABC में, DE, BC के समांतर है, AD = x + 1, DB = 2x, AE = 3x + 2, EC = 5x है। x का मान ज्ञात कीजिए (x &gt; 0)। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2"},"2":{"en":"1"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"290\" height=\"170\" viewBox=\"0 0 290 170\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M120 18L40 150H210ZM80 84L165 84\"/><path d=\"M120 80l5 4-5 4M122 146l5 4-5 4\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"120\" y=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"154\">B</text><text x=\"214\" y=\"154\">C</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"88\">D</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"88\">E</text><text x=\"93\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"end\">x + 1</text><text x=\"53\" y=\"121\" text-anchor=\"end\">2x</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"55\">3x + 2</text><text x=\"194\" y=\"121\">5x</text></g></svg><br>By Basic Proportionality Theorem: \\(\\frac{AD}{DB} = \\frac{AE}{EC}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{x + 1}{2x} = \\frac{3x + 2}{5x}\\)<br>\\(5(x + 1) = 2(3x + 2) \\Rightarrow 5x + 5 = 6x + 4\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 1.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"290\" height=\"170\" viewBox=\"0 0 290 170\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M120 18L40 150H210ZM80 84L165 84\"/><path d=\"M120 80l5 4-5 4M122 146l5 4-5 4\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"120\" y=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"154\">B</text><text x=\"214\" y=\"154\">C</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"88\">D</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"88\">E</text><text x=\"93\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"end\">x + 1</text><text x=\"53\" y=\"121\" text-anchor=\"end\">2x</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"55\">3x + 2</text><text x=\"194\" y=\"121\">5x</text></g></svg><br>आधारभूत समानुपातिकता प्रमेय से: \\(\\frac{AD}{DB} = \\frac{AE}{EC}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{x + 1}{2x} = \\frac{3x + 2}{5x}\\)<br>\\(5(x + 1) = 2(3x + 2) \\Rightarrow 5x + 5 = 6x + 4\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000074347","section":"MATH","topic":"Percentage","question":{"en":"A corporate consultant is taxed under a progressive annual income model:<br>• Earnings up to ₹10,00,000 are taxed at a base rate of 10%.<br>• Any earnings exceeding ₹10,00,000 are taxed at a higher rate of 25%.<br>If the consultant paid a total annual income tax of exactly ₹2,50,000, what percentage of their total gross income was paid as tax? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक कॉरपोरेट सलाहकार पर प्रगतिशील वार्षिक आय मॉडल के अंतर्गत कर लगाया जाता है:<br>• ₹10,00,000 तक की आय पर 10% की आधार दर से कर लगता है।<br>• ₹10,00,000 से अधिक की किसी भी आय पर 25% की उच्च दर से कर लगता है।<br>यदि सलाहकार ने कुल ठीक ₹2,50,000 वार्षिक आयकर चुकाया, तो उसकी कुल सकल आय का कितना प्रतिशत कर के रूप में चुकाया गया? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12.505%"},"2":{"en":"18.625%"},"3":{"en":"10.025%"},"4":{"en":"15.625%"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Tax on first ₹10,00,000 = 10% = ₹1,00,000<br>Remaining tax = ₹1,50,000 at 25% → income above 10 lakh = \\(\\frac{150000}{0.25} = \\) ₹6,00,000<br>Total income = ₹16,00,000<br>Tax % = \\(\\frac{2.5}{16} \\times 100 = \\boxed{15.625\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 15.625%.</b>","hi":"पहले ₹10,00,000 पर कर = 10% = ₹1,00,000<br>शेष कर = ₹1,50,000, 25% की दर से → 10 लाख से अधिक आय = \\(\\frac{150000}{0.25} = \\) ₹6,00,000<br>कुल आय = ₹16,00,000<br>कर % = \\(\\frac{2.5}{16} \\times 100 = \\boxed{15.625\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 15.625% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000074348","section":"MATH","topic":"Mixture and Alligation","question":{"en":"An artisan in Shantiniketan is preparing a large vat of natural indigo dye for traditional Batik fabrics. The vat initially contains 80 liters of a dye-to-water mixture in the ratio 3:13. To achieve a deeper and richer colour, the artisan boils the mixture to evaporate some of the water. Once done, the new ratio of dye to water in the vat is 1:3. How many liters of water were evaporated during the boiling process? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"शांतिनिकेतन का एक कारीगर पारंपरिक बाटिक कपड़ों के लिए प्राकृतिक नील रंग का एक बड़ा कुंड तैयार कर रहा है। कुंड में शुरू में 80 लीटर रंग और पानी का मिश्रण 3:13 के अनुपात में है। गहरा और समृद्ध रंग पाने के लिए, कारीगर मिश्रण को उबालता है ताकि कुछ पानी वाष्पित हो जाए। इसके बाद, कुंड में रंग और पानी का नया अनुपात 1:3 हो जाता है। उबालने की प्रक्रिया में कितने लीटर पानी वाष्पित हुआ? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"20 liters","hi":"20 लीटर"},"2":{"en":"21 liters","hi":"21 लीटर"},"3":{"en":"22 liters","hi":"22 लीटर"},"4":{"en":"24 liters","hi":"24 लीटर"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Dye = \\(\\frac{3}{16} \\times 80 = 15\\) L, Water = 65 L<br>Dye stays same. New ratio 1 : 3 → Water = \\(15 \\times 3 = 45\\) L<br>Water evaporated = \\(65 - 45 = \\boxed{20}\\) L<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 20 liters.</b>","hi":"रंग = \\(\\frac{3}{16} \\times 80 = 15\\) L, पानी = 65 L<br>रंग की मात्रा समान रहती है। नया अनुपात 1 : 3 → पानी = \\(15 \\times 3 = 45\\) L<br>वाष्पित पानी = \\(65 - 45 = \\boxed{20}\\) L<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 20 लीटर है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000074349","section":"MATH","topic":"Pipe and Cistern","question":{"en":"A server's storage drive is at 0% capacity. A malicious script begins flooding it with junk data at a rate that would completely fill the drive in 6 hours. 3 hours since the attack starts, the IT team activates Scrubber A, which by itself can delete a full drive of data in 15 hours. 2 hours after the activation of A, they also turn on Scrubber B, which can delete a full drive in 5 hours. If the script runs continuously, at what exact time will the drive return to being 100% empty, if the attack started at 12:00 PM (noon)? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक सर्वर की स्टोरेज ड्राइव 0% भरी हुई है। एक दुर्भावनापूर्ण स्क्रिप्ट इसमें इस दर से जंक डेटा भरना शुरू करती है कि ड्राइव 6 घंटे में पूरी भर जाए। हमला शुरू होने के 3 घंटे बाद, IT टीम स्क्रबर A को चालू करती है, जो अकेले एक पूरी ड्राइव का डेटा 15 घंटे में हटा सकता है। A के चालू होने के 2 घंटे बाद, वे स्क्रबर B को भी चालू करते हैं, जो एक पूरी ड्राइव 5 घंटे में खाली कर सकता है। यदि स्क्रिप्ट लगातार चलती रहे और हमला दोपहर 12:00 PM पर शुरू हुआ हो, तो ड्राइव ठीक किस समय फिर से 100% खाली होगी? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"7:00 PM"},"2":{"en":"10:30 PM"},"3":{"en":"12:00 AM (midnight)","hi":"12:00 AM (मध्यरात्रि)"},"4":{"en":"12:30 AM"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Capacity = LCM(6, 15, 5) = 30 units<br>Script = +5/hr, A = −2/hr, B = −6/hr<br>12 PM–3 PM: \\(5 \\times 3 = 15\\) units<br>3 PM–5 PM: \\((5 - 2) \\times 2 = 6\\) → 21 units<br>After 5 PM: net = \\(5 - 2 - 6 = -3\\)/hr → time = \\(\\frac{21}{3} = 7\\) hr<br>Drive empty at 5 PM + 7 hr = \\(\\boxed{12:00}\\) AM (midnight)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 12:00 AM (midnight).</b>","hi":"क्षमता = LCM(6, 15, 5) = 30 इकाई<br>स्क्रिप्ट = +5/घंटा, A = −2/घंटा, B = −6/घंटा<br>12 PM–3 PM: \\(5 \\times 3 = 15\\) इकाई<br>3 PM–5 PM: \\((5 - 2) \\times 2 = 6\\) → 21 इकाई<br>5 PM के बाद: शुद्ध दर = \\(5 - 2 - 6 = -3\\)/घंटा → समय = \\(\\frac{21}{3} = 7\\) घंटे<br>ड्राइव खाली होगी 5 PM + 7 घंटे = \\(\\boxed{12:00}\\) AM (मध्यरात्रि)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 12:00 AM (मध्यरात्रि) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000074350","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"Solve for acute \\(\\theta\\): \\(\\tan(\\theta + 24^\\circ) = \\cot(\\theta - 12^\\circ)\\) [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"न्यून कोण \\(\\theta\\) के लिए हल कीजिए: \\(\\tan(\\theta + 24^\\circ) = \\cot(\\theta - 12^\\circ)\\) [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"36°"},"2":{"en":"33°"},"3":{"en":"39°"},"4":{"en":"42°"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"If \\(\\tan A = \\cot B\\), then \\(A + B = 90^\\circ\\)<br>\\((\\theta + 24^\\circ) + (\\theta - 12^\\circ) = 90^\\circ\\)<br>\\(2\\theta = 78^\\circ \\Rightarrow \\theta = \\boxed{39^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 39°.</b>","hi":"यदि \\(\\tan A = \\cot B\\) हो, तो \\(A + B = 90^\\circ\\)<br>\\((\\theta + 24^\\circ) + (\\theta - 12^\\circ) = 90^\\circ\\)<br>\\(2\\theta = 78^\\circ \\Rightarrow \\theta = \\boxed{39^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 39° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000074351","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"In a right triangle XYZ with \\(\\angle Y = 90^\\circ\\), if \\(\\angle X = 2\\angle Z\\), find cos X. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक समकोण त्रिभुज XYZ में \\(\\angle Y = 90^\\circ\\) है, यदि \\(\\angle X = 2\\angle Z\\) है, तो cos X ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{3}\\)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"137\" height=\"165\" viewBox=\"0 0 137 165\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M22 141H92V20Z\"/><path d=\"M83 141v-9h9\"/><path d=\"M44 141A22 22 0 0 0 33 122\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"8\" y=\"155\">X</text><text x=\"94\" y=\"155\">Y</text><text x=\"96\" y=\"24\">Z</text><text x=\"48\" y=\"136\">60°</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\angle X + \\angle Z = 90^\\circ \\Rightarrow 2\\angle Z + \\angle Z = 90^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\angle Z = 30^\\circ,\\ \\angle X = 60^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\cos X = \\cos 60^\\circ = \\boxed{\\frac{1}{2}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\).</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"137\" height=\"165\" viewBox=\"0 0 137 165\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M22 141H92V20Z\"/><path d=\"M83 141v-9h9\"/><path d=\"M44 141A22 22 0 0 0 33 122\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"8\" y=\"155\">X</text><text x=\"94\" y=\"155\">Y</text><text x=\"96\" y=\"24\">Z</text><text x=\"48\" y=\"136\">60°</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\angle X + \\angle Z = 90^\\circ \\Rightarrow 2\\angle Z + \\angle Z = 90^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\angle Z = 30^\\circ,\\ \\angle X = 60^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\cos X = \\cos 60^\\circ = \\boxed{\\frac{1}{2}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000074352","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Evaluate: \\(103^2 - 97^2\\) [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मान ज्ञात कीजिए: \\(103^2 - 97^2\\) [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1121"},"2":{"en":"1320"},"3":{"en":"1200"},"4":{"en":"1424"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(a^2 - b^2 = (a + b)(a - b)\\)<br>\\(103^2 - 97^2 = 200 \\times 6 = \\boxed{1200}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 1200.</b>","hi":"\\(a^2 - b^2 = (a + b)(a - b)\\)<br>\\(103^2 - 97^2 = 200 \\times 6 = \\boxed{1200}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 1200 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000074353","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(x + \\frac{1}{x} = 6\\), find the value of \\(x^5 + \\frac{1}{x^5}\\). [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(x + \\frac{1}{x} = 6\\) है, तो \\(x^5 + \\frac{1}{x^5}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"6276"},"2":{"en":"2726"},"3":{"en":"6726"},"4":{"en":"7662"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = 6^2 - 2 = 34\\)<br>\\(x^3 + \\frac{1}{x^3} = 6^3 - 3 \\times 6 = 198\\)<br>\\(x^5 + \\frac{1}{x^5} = \\left(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2}\\right)\\left(x^3 + \\frac{1}{x^3}\\right) - \\left(x + \\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\)<br>\\(= 34 \\times 198 - 6 = 6732 - 6 = \\boxed{6726}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 6726.</b>","hi":"\\(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = 6^2 - 2 = 34\\)<br>\\(x^3 + \\frac{1}{x^3} = 6^3 - 3 \\times 6 = 198\\)<br>\\(x^5 + \\frac{1}{x^5} = \\left(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2}\\right)\\left(x^3 + \\frac{1}{x^3}\\right) - \\left(x + \\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\)<br>\\(= 34 \\times 198 - 6 = 6732 - 6 = \\boxed{6726}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 6726 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000074354","section":"MATH","topic":"Mixture and Alligation","question":{"en":"A tank contains 600 litres of an aqueous solution with a 40% salt concentration by volume. Assume that the component volumes are perfectly additive (mixing causes no volume contraction), and that the solution is thoroughly stirred to maintain complete homogeneity after each step. The following sequential operations are performed:<br>• 120 litres of the solution is removed and replaced with an equal volume of pure water.<br>• This exact replacement process is repeated once more.<br>• Then, 60 litres of the resulting solution is removed and replaced with an equal volume of liquid pure salt solute.<br>What is the final percentage of salt by volume in the resulting mixture? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक टंकी में 600 लीटर जलीय विलयन है जिसमें आयतन के अनुसार 40% नमक है। मान लीजिए कि घटकों के आयतन पूरी तरह योगात्मक हैं (मिलाने से आयतन में कोई संकुचन नहीं होता), और हर चरण के बाद विलयन को अच्छी तरह हिलाया जाता है ताकि वह पूरी तरह समांगी रहे। निम्नलिखित क्रमिक संक्रियाएँ की जाती हैं:<br>• 120 लीटर विलयन निकालकर उतनी ही मात्रा में शुद्ध पानी मिलाया जाता है।<br>• यही प्रतिस्थापन प्रक्रिया एक बार और दोहराई जाती है।<br>• फिर, परिणामी विलयन का 60 लीटर निकालकर उतनी ही मात्रा में शुद्ध तरल नमक विलेय मिलाया जाता है।<br>परिणामी मिश्रण में आयतन के अनुसार नमक का अंतिम प्रतिशत क्या है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"23.04%"},"2":{"en":"25.60%"},"3":{"en":"33.04%"},"4":{"en":"35.60%"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Salt initially = 40% of 600 = 240 L<br>After two replacements by water: \\(240 \\times \\left(1 - \\frac{120}{600}\\right)^2 = 240 \\times \\frac{16}{25} = 153.6\\) L<br>Remove 60 L (\\(\\frac{1}{10}\\)): salt left = \\(153.6 \\times \\frac{9}{10} = 138.24\\) L<br>Add 60 L pure salt: salt = 198.24 L<br>Salt % = \\(\\frac{198.24}{600} \\times 100 = \\boxed{33.04\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 33.04%.</b>","hi":"प्रारंभ में नमक = 600 का 40% = 240 L<br>पानी से दो बार प्रतिस्थापन के बाद: \\(240 \\times \\left(1 - \\frac{120}{600}\\right)^2 = 240 \\times \\frac{16}{25} = 153.6\\) L<br>60 L (\\(\\frac{1}{10}\\)) निकालने पर शेष नमक = \\(153.6 \\times \\frac{9}{10} = 138.24\\) L<br>60 L शुद्ध नमक मिलाने पर: नमक = 198.24 L<br>नमक % = \\(\\frac{198.24}{600} \\times 100 = \\boxed{33.04\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 33.04% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000074355","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Consider the following two statements regarding a configuration of two distinct circles:<br>Statement 1: If the distance between the centers of two circles is strictly greater than the sum of their radii, then exactly four common tangents can be drawn to them.<br>Statement 2: If the distance between the centers of two circles is strictly less than the absolute difference of their radii, then no common tangents can be drawn to them.<br>Which of the following is correct? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दो भिन्न वृत्तों की स्थिति के संबंध में निम्नलिखित दो कथनों पर विचार कीजिए:<br>कथन 1: यदि दो वृत्तों के केंद्रों के बीच की दूरी उनकी त्रिज्याओं के योग से निश्चित रूप से अधिक है, तो उन पर ठीक चार उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखाएँ खींची जा सकती हैं।<br>कथन 2: यदि दो वृत्तों के केंद्रों के बीच की दूरी उनकी त्रिज्याओं के अंतर के निरपेक्ष मान से निश्चित रूप से कम है, तो उन पर कोई उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा नहीं खींची जा सकती।<br>निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा सही है? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Statement 1 is true.","hi":"केवल कथन 1 सत्य है।"},"2":{"en":"Only Statement 2 is true.","hi":"केवल कथन 2 सत्य है।"},"3":{"en":"Both Statement 1 and Statement 2 are true.","hi":"कथन 1 और कथन 2 दोनों सत्य हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Neither Statement 1 nor Statement 2 is true.","hi":"न तो कथन 1 और न ही कथन 2 सत्य है।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Statement 1: \\(d \\gt r_1 + r_2\\) → circles lie outside each other → 2 direct + 2 transverse = 4 common tangents ✔<br>Statement 2: \\(d \\lt |r_1 - r_2|\\) → one circle lies inside the other → no common tangent ✔<br>\\(\\boxed{\\text{Both are true}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Both Statement 1 and Statement 2 are true.</b>","hi":"कथन 1: \\(d \\gt r_1 + r_2\\) → वृत्त एक-दूसरे के बाहर हैं → 2 सीधी + 2 अनुप्रस्थ = 4 उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखाएँ ✔<br>कथन 2: \\(d \\lt |r_1 - r_2|\\) → एक वृत्त दूसरे के अंदर है → कोई उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा नहीं ✔<br>\\(\\boxed{\\text{Both are true}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): कथन 1 और कथन 2 दोनों सत्य हैं। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000074356","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the following question, a sentence with a blank is given, followed by five words labeled (1), (2), (3), (4), and (5). Choose the word that fills the blank appropriately in the context of the passage.<br><br>In an era marked by global interconnectedness, emerging infectious diseases (1)___ an unprecedented threat to public health infrastructures worldwide. Pathogens such as novel coronaviruses, antibiotic-resistant bacteria, and zoonotic viruses exploit the vulnerabilities of human mobility, urban overcrowding, and ecological disruption.<br><br>Although medical science has made formidable strides, the unpredictable nature of outbreaks (2)___ persistent difficulties in preparedness and response mechanisms. Adding to the complexity, misinformation proliferated through digital platforms (3)___ the efficacy of public health interventions, sometimes undermining vaccination campaigns and quarantine measures. Efforts to combat emerging diseases must therefore be interdisciplinary, blending epidemiology, behavioral science, and policy innovation.<br><br>One key concept in disease containment is herd immunity, a state wherein a significant portion of a population becomes immune, thereby indirectly shielding vulnerable individuals.<br><br>However, achieving (4)___ herd immunity, whether via vaccination or natural exposure, entails considerable ethical and logistical challenges. Beyond infectious diseases, the surge in non-communicable illnesses such as diabetes and cardiovascular disorders further strains public health systems. An effective response to emerging health threats must prioritize resilience, adaptability, and above all, (5)___ prophylaxis. In the absence of robust, coordinated efforts, humanity risks facing pandemics of greater magnitude and complexity than ever previously recorded.<br><br><br>Choose correct tense/subject-verb. (1) [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"poses"},"2":{"en":"pose"},"3":{"en":"had posed"},"4":{"en":"posing"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The plural subject “emerging infectious diseases” takes “pose.”</b><br>The passage states a present general threat, so simple present is appropriate.<br>“Poses” is singular; “had posed” requires a past reference point.<br>“Posing” cannot be the finite verb in this clause.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): pose.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000074357","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the following question, a sentence with a blank is given, followed by five words labeled (1), (2), (3), (4), and (5). Choose the word that fills the blank appropriately in the context of the passage.<br><br>In an era marked by global interconnectedness, emerging infectious diseases (1)___ an unprecedented threat to public health infrastructures worldwide. Pathogens such as novel coronaviruses, antibiotic-resistant bacteria, and zoonotic viruses exploit the vulnerabilities of human mobility, urban overcrowding, and ecological disruption.<br><br>Although medical science has made formidable strides, the unpredictable nature of outbreaks (2)___ persistent difficulties in preparedness and response mechanisms. Adding to the complexity, misinformation proliferated through digital platforms (3)___ the efficacy of public health interventions, sometimes undermining vaccination campaigns and quarantine measures. Efforts to combat emerging diseases must therefore be interdisciplinary, blending epidemiology, behavioral science, and policy innovation.<br><br>One key concept in disease containment is herd immunity, a state wherein a significant portion of a population becomes immune, thereby indirectly shielding vulnerable individuals.<br><br>However, achieving (4)___ herd immunity, whether via vaccination or natural exposure, entails considerable ethical and logistical challenges. Beyond infectious diseases, the surge in non-communicable illnesses such as diabetes and cardiovascular disorders further strains public health systems. An effective response to emerging health threats must prioritize resilience, adaptability, and above all, (5)___ prophylaxis. In the absence of robust, coordinated efforts, humanity risks facing pandemics of greater magnitude and complexity than ever previously recorded.<br><br><br>Focus on tense and agreement. (2) [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"present"},"2":{"en":"presents"},"3":{"en":"presented"},"4":{"en":"presenting"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The singular head noun “nature” takes “presents.”</b><br>“The unpredictable nature of outbreaks presents persistent difficulties.”<br>“Present” would require a plural subject; “presented” shifts to the past.<br>“Presenting” cannot serve as the finite verb here.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): presents.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000074358","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the following question, a sentence with a blank is given, followed by five words labeled (1), (2), (3), (4), and (5). Choose the word that fills the blank appropriately in the context of the passage.<br><br>In an era marked by global interconnectedness, emerging infectious diseases (1)___ an unprecedented threat to public health infrastructures worldwide. Pathogens such as novel coronaviruses, antibiotic-resistant bacteria, and zoonotic viruses exploit the vulnerabilities of human mobility, urban overcrowding, and ecological disruption.<br><br>Although medical science has made formidable strides, the unpredictable nature of outbreaks (2)___ persistent difficulties in preparedness and response mechanisms. Adding to the complexity, misinformation proliferated through digital platforms (3)___ the efficacy of public health interventions, sometimes undermining vaccination campaigns and quarantine measures. Efforts to combat emerging diseases must therefore be interdisciplinary, blending epidemiology, behavioral science, and policy innovation.<br><br>One key concept in disease containment is herd immunity, a state wherein a significant portion of a population becomes immune, thereby indirectly shielding vulnerable individuals.<br><br>However, achieving (4)___ herd immunity, whether via vaccination or natural exposure, entails considerable ethical and logistical challenges. Beyond infectious diseases, the surge in non-communicable illnesses such as diabetes and cardiovascular disorders further strains public health systems. An effective response to emerging health threats must prioritize resilience, adaptability, and above all, (5)___ prophylaxis. In the absence of robust, coordinated efforts, humanity risks facing pandemics of greater magnitude and complexity than ever previously recorded.<br><br><br>Choose correct word to get appropriate construction. (3) [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"impede"},"2":{"en":"impedes"},"3":{"en":"has impeding"},"4":{"en":"impeding"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Singular “misinformation” takes “impedes.”</b><br>The participle “proliferated through digital platforms” describes misinformation and does not change the subject.<br>“Impede” lacks singular agreement; “has impeding” is ungrammatical.<br>“Impeding” would leave the main clause without a finite verb.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): impedes.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000074359","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the following question, a sentence with a blank is given, followed by five words labeled (1), (2), (3), (4), and (5). Choose the word that fills the blank appropriately in the context of the passage.<br><br>In an era marked by global interconnectedness, emerging infectious diseases (1)___ an unprecedented threat to public health infrastructures worldwide. Pathogens such as novel coronaviruses, antibiotic-resistant bacteria, and zoonotic viruses exploit the vulnerabilities of human mobility, urban overcrowding, and ecological disruption.<br><br>Although medical science has made formidable strides, the unpredictable nature of outbreaks (2)___ persistent difficulties in preparedness and response mechanisms. Adding to the complexity, misinformation proliferated through digital platforms (3)___ the efficacy of public health interventions, sometimes undermining vaccination campaigns and quarantine measures. Efforts to combat emerging diseases must therefore be interdisciplinary, blending epidemiology, behavioral science, and policy innovation.<br><br>One key concept in disease containment is herd immunity, a state wherein a significant portion of a population becomes immune, thereby indirectly shielding vulnerable individuals.<br><br>However, achieving (4)___ herd immunity, whether via vaccination or natural exposure, entails considerable ethical and logistical challenges. Beyond infectious diseases, the surge in non-communicable illnesses such as diabetes and cardiovascular disorders further strains public health systems. An effective response to emerging health threats must prioritize resilience, adaptability, and above all, (5)___ prophylaxis. In the absence of robust, coordinated efforts, humanity risks facing pandemics of greater magnitude and complexity than ever previously recorded.<br><br><br>In this context, “herd immunity” most nearly refers to: (4) [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Immunity achieved only through natural infection"},"2":{"en":"Collective immunity reducing disease transmission"},"3":{"en":"Forced immunity via coercive measures"},"4":{"en":"Immunity affecting only animals"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Herd immunity (सामूहिक प्रतिरक्षा) = widespread immunity that indirectly protects vulnerable people.</b><br>When a significant portion of a population is immune, disease transmission falls.<br>It may arise through vaccination or natural exposure, not only infection.<br>It does not require coercion and is not limited to animals.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Collective immunity reducing disease transmission.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000074360","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the following question, a sentence with a blank is given, followed by five words labeled (1), (2), (3), (4), and (5). Choose the word that fills the blank appropriately in the context of the passage.<br><br>In an era marked by global interconnectedness, emerging infectious diseases (1)___ an unprecedented threat to public health infrastructures worldwide. Pathogens such as novel coronaviruses, antibiotic-resistant bacteria, and zoonotic viruses exploit the vulnerabilities of human mobility, urban overcrowding, and ecological disruption.<br><br>Although medical science has made formidable strides, the unpredictable nature of outbreaks (2)___ persistent difficulties in preparedness and response mechanisms. Adding to the complexity, misinformation proliferated through digital platforms (3)___ the efficacy of public health interventions, sometimes undermining vaccination campaigns and quarantine measures. Efforts to combat emerging diseases must therefore be interdisciplinary, blending epidemiology, behavioral science, and policy innovation.<br><br>One key concept in disease containment is herd immunity, a state wherein a significant portion of a population becomes immune, thereby indirectly shielding vulnerable individuals.<br><br>However, achieving (4)___ herd immunity, whether via vaccination or natural exposure, entails considerable ethical and logistical challenges. Beyond infectious diseases, the surge in non-communicable illnesses such as diabetes and cardiovascular disorders further strains public health systems. An effective response to emerging health threats must prioritize resilience, adaptability, and above all, (5)___ prophylaxis. In the absence of robust, coordinated efforts, humanity risks facing pandemics of greater magnitude and complexity than ever previously recorded.<br><br><br>The word “prophylaxis” most nearly means: (5) [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Treatment after illness"},"2":{"en":"Preventive action against disease"},"3":{"en":"Diagnosis of unknown conditions"},"4":{"en":"Rehabilitation and therapy"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Prophylaxis (रोकथाम) = action taken to prevent disease.</b><br>Public health prioritizes preventive action before illness occurs.<br>Treatment after illness and rehabilitation follow disease rather than prevent it.<br>Diagnosis identifies a condition and is not prophylaxis.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Preventive action against disease.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000074361","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Choose the correct indirect speech form of the sentence below.<br>The science instructor said, “Water turns into ice at 0 degrees Celsius.” [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The science instructor said that water turned into ice at 0 degrees Celsius."},"2":{"en":"The science instructor said that water turns into ice at 0 degrees Celsius"},"3":{"en":"The science instructor said that water had turned into ice at 0 degrees Celsius."},"4":{"en":"The science instructor told that water turns into ice at 0 degrees Celsius."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Universal scientific facts remain in the present tense in reported speech.</b><br>Water freezing at 0°C is a general truth, so “turns” does not change.<br>A and C unnecessarily backshift the tense.<br>D incorrectly uses “told” without an object.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): The science instructor said that water turns into ice at 0 degrees Celsius.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000074362","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Which of the following is the correct direct speech form of the given sentence?<br>Chayanika wanted to know if Garry had selected those candidates for the interview. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Chayanika asked, “Did Garry select these candidates for the interview?”"},"2":{"en":"Chayanika asked, “Did Garry select those candidates for the interview?”"},"3":{"en":"Chayanika asked, “Had Garry selected these candidates for the interview?”"},"4":{"en":"Chayanika asked, “Has Garry selected these candidates for the interview?”"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Reported past perfect can return to present perfect, and “those” becomes “these.”</b><br>“Had selected” therefore becomes “Has Garry selected.”<br>A and B use simple past, while C retains past perfect.<br>B also retains the distal demonstrative “those.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Chayanika asked, “Has Garry selected these candidates for the interview?”.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000074363","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blanks with the appropriate article.<br>___ apple fell from ___ tree, which was during ___ summer season. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"An, the, the"},"2":{"en":"A, the, an"},"3":{"en":"An, an, the"},"4":{"en":"The, the, the"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Use “an” before a vowel sound and “the” for specific reference.</b><br>“Apple” begins with a vowel sound, so the first blank takes “An.”<br>The tree and summer season are specified in the sentence, so both take “the.”<br>“A apple” and “an tree” are incorrect.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): An, the, the.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000074364","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Change the following sentence into indirect speech.<br>“I shall be 16 tomorrow,” said Tanuka. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Tanuka said that she will be 16 tomorrow."},"2":{"en":"Tanuka said that she shall be 16 tomorrow."},"3":{"en":"Tanuka said that she would be 16 the next day."},"4":{"en":"Tanuka said that she would be 16 tomorrow."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Shall” becomes “would,” and “tomorrow” becomes “the next day.”</b><br>“I” changes to “she.”<br>A and B retain the original modal; D retains “tomorrow.”<br>C makes all required reporting changes.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Tanuka said that she would be 16 the next day.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000074365","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br>As geopolitical tensions reshaped international diplomacy,<br>P. as emerging economies sought to assert greater influence in global decision-making,<br>Q. leading to the realignment of trade agreements and defense partnerships<br>R. traditional alliances among major world powers faced significant strain,<br>S. while long-standing institutions like the United Nations and G7 faced calls for reform [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"RPSQ"},"2":{"en":"RPQS"},"3":{"en":"PRSQ"},"4":{"en":"SQRP"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: RPQS</b><br>R supplies the main clause about strain on traditional alliances.<br>P explains the pressure from emerging economies.<br>Q gives the resulting realignment, and S adds reform pressure on international institutions.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): RPQS.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000074366","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with an appropriate degree of comparison.<br>When comparing the two theories, Newton's laws were initially considered ___ acceptable. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"least"},"2":{"en":"less"},"3":{"en":"lesser"},"4":{"en":"little"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Use the comparative “less” when comparing two things.</b><br>Newton’s laws were considered less acceptable than the competing theory.<br>“Least” is superlative and requires more than two items.<br>“Lesser” generally modifies nouns, while “little” is the positive degree.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): less.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000074367","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"What does the idiom “All his ventures went to the winds” mean? [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"All his efforts were wasted"},"2":{"en":"He became very successful"},"3":{"en":"He changed his business frequently"},"4":{"en":"His ventures were well-organized"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Go to the winds (बेकार हो जाना) = be wasted or come to nothing.</b><br>The idiom means all his ventures and efforts failed.<br>Example: “After the fraud was exposed, his investments went to the winds.”<br>Success and organization are contrary; frequent change is not implied.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): All his efforts were wasted.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000074368","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Choose the error in the sentence.<br>The teacher emphasized on the importance of time management. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"on"},"2":{"en":"emphasized"},"3":{"en":"management"},"4":{"en":"importance"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Emphasize” is a transitive verb and takes a direct object without “on.”</b><br>The erroneous word is “on.”<br>Correct sentence: “The teacher <b>emphasized</b> the importance of time management.”<br>The remaining words are correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): on.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000074369","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br>The transboundary conservation program<br>P. through joint international efforts<br>Q. that traverse national borders<br>R. protects migratory species<br>S. by creating safe corridors [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"PRSQ"},"2":{"en":"RQSP"},"3":{"en":"SPQR"},"4":{"en":"RPQS"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: RQSP</b><br>R gives the predicate “protects migratory species”.<br>Q must come right after “species”, since it describes them: “that traverse national borders”.<br>S gives the method: “by creating safe corridors”.<br>P closes with how the corridors are created: “through joint international efforts”.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): RQSP.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000074370","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Which of the given options arranges the following sentences in the most logical sequence to form a meaningful paragraph?<br>1. Socialization is the process by which individuals learn and internalize the values, beliefs, and norms of their society.<br>2. Role theory explains how individuals occupy different roles in society and how their behavior is shaped by these roles.<br>3. The process of socialization is critical for an individual’s development and is influenced by various agents like family, peers, and media.<br>4. The roles people play, such as being a student, parent, or worker, come with expectations that guide their actions and interactions.<br>5. Through socialization, individuals learn to perform specific social roles within their community. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3-5-4-1-2"},"2":{"en":"2-5-4-3-1"},"3":{"en":"1-4-3-2-5"},"4":{"en":"1-3-5-2-4"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 1-3-5-2-4</b><br>Sentence 1 defines socialization, and sentence 3 explains its importance and agents.<br>Sentence 5 links socialization to social roles; sentence 2 introduces role theory.<br>Sentence 4 concludes with examples and expectations attached to roles.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 1-3-5-2-4.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000074371","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Which of the given options arranges the following sentences in the most logical sequence to form a meaningful paragraph?<br>1. Mythology played a vital role in early societies by explaining natural events and human existence.<br>2. Over time, mythology evolved, influencing literature, art and philosophy.<br>3. Many ancient civilizations, such as the Greeks and Egyptians, used myths to explain the origins of the world.<br>4. These myths were often passed down orally, shaping cultural traditions and religious beliefs. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4-2-3-1"},"2":{"en":"2-3-4-1"},"3":{"en":"3-4-2-1"},"4":{"en":"1-3-4-2"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 1-3-4-2</b><br>Sentence 1 introduces mythology’s early explanatory role.<br>Sentence 3 gives civilizations as examples, and sentence 4 describes the transmission of “these myths.”<br>Sentence 2 concludes with mythology’s later cultural influence.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 1-3-4-2.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000074372","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate synonym of the given word: <b>EXPEDITE</b> [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Delay"},"2":{"en":"Hasten"},"3":{"en":"Obstruct"},"4":{"en":"Prolong"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Expedite (शीघ्र करना) = make an action or process happen sooner.</b><br><b>Delay (विलंब करना)</b> = make late<br><b>Hasten (शीघ्र करना)</b> = accelerate ✔<br><b>Obstruct (रोकना)</b> = block progress<br><b>Prolong (लंबा करना)</b> = extend in time<br>More synonyms: accelerate, facilitate, speed up.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Hasten.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000074373","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom:<br>Man of straw [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A person of high emotional strength"},"2":{"en":"A confident negotiator"},"3":{"en":"A highly rigid and disciplined man"},"4":{"en":"A weak or ineffectual person"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Man of straw (कमजोर या प्रभावहीन व्यक्ति)</b><br>It means a person of little substance, strength or influence.<br>Example: “He merely acts as a man of straw for the real decision-makers.”<br>Emotional strength, confident negotiation and discipline are not suggested.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): A weak or ineffectual person.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000074374","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Find the part of the sentence that contains an error:<br>Each of the candidates (1)/ are expected to carry (2)/ their original ID proofs (3)/ for verification. (4)/ [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"(1)"},"2":{"en":"(2)"},"3":{"en":"(3)"},"4":{"en":"(4)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Each” is singular and takes a singular verb.</b><br>Part (2) should read “<b>is expected</b> to carry,” not “are expected.”<br>The plural “candidates” does not control agreement after “each of.”<br>The other parts are correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): (2).</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000074375","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Change the following from active to passive:<br>They were cleaning the hall for the function. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The hall was cleaned for the function."},"2":{"en":"The hall is being cleaned for the function."},"3":{"en":"The hall was being cleaned for the function."},"4":{"en":"The hall has been cleaned for the function."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Past continuous passive = was/were being + past participle.</b><br>The singular object “the hall” takes “was being cleaned.”<br>A changes to simple past, B to present continuous, and D to present perfect.<br>The purpose phrase “for the function” remains unchanged.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): The hall was being cleaned for the function.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000074376","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Change the following from active to passive:<br>Lightning struck the tree. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The tree had been struck by lightning."},"2":{"en":"The tree was struck by lightning."},"3":{"en":"The tree is struck by lightning."},"4":{"en":"The tree has been struck by lightning."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Simple past passive = was/were + past participle.</b><br>The singular object “the tree” becomes the subject.<br>Correct form: “The tree <b>was struck</b> by lightning.”<br>A uses past perfect, C simple present, and D present perfect.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): The tree was struck by lightning.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000074377","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Convert the sentence provided below from its passive voice structure to an active voice structure:<br>She was heard being scolded by the principal during the assembly. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The principal heard her being scolded during assembly."},"2":{"en":"Someone heard the principal scolding her during the assembly."},"3":{"en":"She was scolding the principal, who was heard during assembly."},"4":{"en":"People heard the principal being scolded by her during the assembly."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The unnamed hearer becomes “someone,” and “being scolded by the principal” becomes “the principal scolding her.”</b><br>The principal is the person administering the scolding.<br>A makes the principal the hearer; C and D reverse who scolds whom.<br>B preserves both relationships and the time reference.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Someone heard the principal scolding her during the assembly.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000074378","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Convert the sentence provided below from its passive voice structure to an active voice structure:<br>The guest was believed to have been misinformed about the schedule. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"It was believed that the guest had been misinformed about the schedule."},"2":{"en":"Someone had misinformed the guest, as it was believed."},"3":{"en":"It is believed the guest misinformed others."},"4":{"en":"The schedule was believed to misinform the guest."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Recast the passive infinitive as a finite clause without changing the belief.</b><br>Option A preserves the belief that the guest had received incorrect schedule information.<br>B changes the structure and timing awkwardly; C makes the guest misinform others.<br>D illogically assigns intention to the schedule.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): It was believed that the guest had been misinformed about the schedule.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000074379","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the highlighted part of the sentence:<br>He <b>is living</b> here since 2010. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"is living here from"},"2":{"en":"has been living here since"},"3":{"en":"lives here since"},"4":{"en":"was living here since"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Present perfect continuous expresses an action continuing from a past point to the present.</b><br>“Since 2010” gives the starting point.<br>Correct sentence: “He <b>has been living</b> here since 2010.”<br>Simple present and past continuous do not convey the correct continuing time frame.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): has been living here since.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000074380","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"A sentence is provided in indirect speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding direct speech.<br>She said that barely had she stepped out when it began to rain. [SSC CGL 12/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"“Barely had I stepped out when it began to rain,” she said."},"2":{"en":"“I had barely stepped out when it started to rain,” said she."},"3":{"en":"“It started raining as soon as I stepped out,” she said."},"4":{"en":"“I barely stepped out and it rained,” she said."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Restore “she” to “I” while retaining negative adverbial inversion.</b><br>“Barely had she stepped out” becomes “Barely had I stepped out.”<br>B changes inversion and wording; C replaces the correlative structure with “as soon as.”<br>D loses both the inversion and the immediate time relationship.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): “Barely had I stepped out when it began to rain,” she said.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};